            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biopsych.2022.12.018> ;
            slr:claim_label "Site effects were harmonised using ComBat." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Single 0.601(0.064) 0.648(0.065) 0.695(0.108) 0.571(0.100) Ensemble 0.611(0.012) 0.638(0.054) 0.654(0.088) 0.634(0.064) Fed 0.647(0.049) 0.728(0.073) 0.849(0.124) 0.712(0.075) Fed-MoE 0.671(0.082) 0.728(0.083) 0.809(0.098) 0.744(0.130) Fed-Align 0.676(0.071) 0.751(0.053) 0.829(0.091) 0.712(0.089) Mix 0.671(0.035) 0.740(0.063) 0.829(0.137) 0.710(0.128) Table 3: Results of using diﬀerent training strategies" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.media.2020.101765> ;
            slr:claim_label "Per-site classification accuracies for Single, Ensemble, Fed, Fed-MoE, Fed-Align and Mix strategies using the Harvard-Oxford atlas." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """Twenty-six participants had excessive head motion on their fMRI scan (>4 mm maximum absolute 
20 
displacement).""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dcn.2019.100747> ;
            slr:claim_label "A quantitative motion-exclusion threshold (>4mm maximum absolute displacement) removed 26 participants." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """Therefore, we divided the ABIDE dataset into training and test sets by ran-
domly selecting a label-balanced 889 (4/5) of the ABIDE subjects as the training set, leaving
the remaining 222 (1/5) ABIDE subjects as the testing set.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0166934> ;
            slr:claim_label "The ABIDE dataset was randomly split into a label-balanced 889-subject training set and a 222-subject hold-out test set." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """The ﬁrst phase of ABIDE (ABIDE-I)
compiles a dataset of 1112 individuals from 17 sites and
consists of 539 individuals with ASD and 573 typical controls. 
Since the scan parameters vary across sites, ABIDE is a highly
heterogeneous dataset. To avoid the impact of data heterogeneity,
we collected raw rs-fMRI data from the whole NYU site,
consisting of 79 ASD subjects and 105 normal controls (NCs).""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnhum.2021.687288> ;
            slr:claim_label "To avoid cross-site heterogeneity, the study restricted analysis to the single NYU site of ABIDE-I (79 ASD, 105 NC) rather than the full 539/573 ABIDE-I sample." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "we demonstrate the model performance on the functional connectivity graphs of 871 subjects from the challenging Autism Brain Imaging Data Exchange (ABIDE) database [5], which contains heterogeneous rs-fMRI data acquired at multiple" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-66182-7_54> ;
            slr:claim_label "Study uses the 871-subject ABIDE I cohort." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """The code is available
at https://github.com/LYQbyte/ASD-HNet.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neunet.2025.107450> ;
            slr:claim_label "The authors' code is publicly released on GitHub." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.7"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The resting-state fMRI data of 41 ASD and 41 normal control (NC) cases were gathered from the Autism Brain  Image Data Exchange (ABIDE) sources [16], taken from multiple independent neuroimaging sites." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.30880/ijie.2021.13.05.006> ;
            slr:claim_label "Final sample confirmed as 41 ASD/41 NC across independent sites." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.7"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """For the resting-state functional brain scans in ABIDE, we built on data previously made
available by the Preprocessed Connectomes initiative (http://preprocessed-connectomes-
project.org/abide). The preprocessing was performed with C-PAC (https://fcp-indi.github.io)
and included slice time correction, head motion correction, skull stripping, and intensity nor-
malization. The rs-fMRI data were detrended and adjusted for common nuisance effects
related to head motion, white matter, and cerebrospinal fluid signals using CompCor [58], fol-
lowed by band-pass filtering (0.01 to 0.1 Hz).""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3001627> ;
            slr:claim_label "ABIDE rs-fMRI was preprocessed via the Preprocessed Connectomes initiative using C-PAC (slice-time correction, motion correction, skull stripping, intensity normalization, CompCor, band-pass filtering)." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "We specifically focused on the regional homogeneity (ReHo) fMRI derivative (Zang et al. 2004) from the Configurable Pipeline for the Analysis of Connectomes (CPAC) pipeline (Craddock et al. 2013)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3897/rio.3.e12733> ;
            slr:claim_label "Feature was the ReHo derivative from the C-PAC pipeline (Preprocessed Connectomes Project release)." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The ABIDE dataset contains 539 individuals with ASD and 573 control subjects." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3897/rio.3.e12733> ;
            slr:claim_label "Cohort used was the full ABIDE I preprocessed dataset: 539 ASD, 573 controls." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """(1) Discarding the first 5 volumes. (2) Correct-
ing of slice-related delay. (3) Correcting head movement.
(4) Using EPI template normalization in MNI space, resam-
pling to 3 mm resolution of 3 × 3 × 3. (5) Smoothing with a
4 mm full-width at half-maximum (FWHM) Gaussian ker-
nel. (6) Linear detrending and temporal band-pass filter-
ing of BOLD signal (0.01-0.10 Hz).""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neunet.2025.107450> ;
            slr:claim_label "DPARSF preprocessing steps: discard first 5 volumes, slice-timing, head-movement correction, normalization, smoothing, band-pass filtering." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "TD > ASD group differences remained similar in the secondary ‘scrubbed’ analyses (Supplementary Figure S4B), whereas primary findings of ASD > TD group differences were only identified subthreshold." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1093/scan/nst156> ;
            slr:claim_label "A secondary motion-scrubbing sensitivity analysis of the ABIDE data showed the TD>ASD findings remained similar, while ASD>TD findings were only subthreshold." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.75"^^xsd:float ],
