            slr:relevance_score "0.7"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The 240 regions of interest (ROIs) defined for this study were extracted from the TT_Daemon human brain atlas [43] provided with the AFNI package [44]." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0190081> ;
            slr:claim_label "ROI analysis used the TT_Daemon atlas via AFNI." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.7"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "the preprocessed multimodal MRI features were jointly analyzed by a fusion-with-reference model called “MCCAR + jICA”" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1186/s13229-020-00397-4> ;
            slr:claim_label "Fusion of fALFF and GM voxel maps used MCCAR+jICA, guided by ADOS scores." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The accuracy of our model without any dimensionality reduction or feature selection was ~ 62%." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3897/rio.3.e12733> ;
            slr:claim_label "Whole-brain voxel-wise ReHo SVM/logistic classifier achieved about 62% accuracy with no feature selection/dimensionality reduction." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """Briefly, we selected cases between 
7 and 18 years of age (the ages most represented across 
ABIDE sites), with MRI data successfully completing 
brain image co-registration and transformation to stand-
ard space, with FIQ between 70 and 148 and with mean 
framewise displacement (mFD) [54] within three times 
the interquartile range (IQR) + the third quartile (Q3) of 
the sample (i.e., mFD 0.39""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1186/s13229-021-00415-z> ;
            slr:claim_label "Cases were selected aged 7-18 years with successful registration, FIQ 70-148, and mFD within 3xIQR+Q3 of the sample (~0.39mm)." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Preprocessing for functional images consisted of realignment for motion correction, slice-timing correction, normalization to the standard MNI space, and smoothing with a 4-mm full width at half- maximum ﬁlter." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnhum.2018.00454> ;
            slr:claim_label "Preprocessing pipeline (CONN toolbox/SPM12-based, not CPAC/DPARSF)." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """After preprocessing (described in section 2.2.), the
ABIDE I dataset was composed of 432 subjects with TD
(348 males, mean age ± standard deviation of 18.21 ±
8.04) and 276 individuals with ASD (241 males, 18.42 ±
8.38). The ABIDE II dataset was composed of 316 subjects
with TD (208 males, 12.80 ± 5.61) and 269 individuals
with ASD (234 males, 13.93 ± 7.07).""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnsys.2018.00074> ;
            slr:claim_label "After preprocessing, ABIDE I yielded 432 TD and 276 ASD subjects (708 total); ABIDE II yielded 316 TD and 269 ASD subjects (585 total)." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """Further, we observed that an estimated RSN entropy model
signiﬁcantly distinguished ASD from controls (p = 0.01) and was associated with level of
ASD symptom severity (p = 0.003).""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2018.00869> ;
            slr:claim_label "The entropy-model fit (not diagnosis-trained) significantly differed between ASD and control groups and correlated with ASD symptom severity." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """we performed a 10-
fold stratiﬁed cross-validation strategy on the two datasets.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41398-024-02972-2> ;
            slr:claim_label "Validation: 10-fold stratified cross-validation." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """Four hundred and ﬁfty-four subjects with complete phenotypic
data were selected from the Autism Brain Imaging Data
Exchange (ABIDE) database (http://fcon_1000.projects.nitrc.
org/indi/abide/index.html). The sample consisted of 256 HC, 166
subjects with autism, and 32 subjects with Asperger’s.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fams.2018.00025> ;
            slr:claim_label "ABIDE cohort: 454 subjects with complete phenotypic data (256 HC, 166 autism, 32 Asperger’s); PDD-NOS excluded." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """The original contributions presented in the
study are included
in the article/supplementary material, further inquiries can be
directed to the corresponding author/s.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fninf.2021.802305> ;
            slr:claim_label "Data availability statement: data in article/supplement, further inquiries to corresponding author." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.3"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "had maximal head motion of less than 5 mm and 5 degrees, and mean framewise displacement (FD) (1) of less than 0.5 mm" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biopsych.2021.12.004> ;
            slr:claim_label "QC excluded scans with head motion >5mm/5deg or mean FD >0.5mm." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Between-group differences were observed in the composition of default-mode and a ventro- temporal-limbic (VTL) subnetwork." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1002/hbm.23084> ;
            slr:claim_label "In the primary (non-ABIDE) movie-watching sample, ASD vs. typical subjects differed in default-mode and ventro-temporal-limbic subnetwork composition." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.5"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The features were standard scaled by the mean and standard deviation of the IMPAC dataset." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-022-06459-2> ;
            slr:claim_label "ABIDE features were scaled using the IMPAC (training) dataset's mean/SD, not refit on ABIDE itself, limiting cross-dataset leakage." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """The best CNN model in this project was 
achieved by ResNet50, with an accuracy of 87.0%.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.11113/jurnalteknologi.v83.16389> ;
            slr:claim_label "ResNet-50 was identified as the best-performing model at 87.0% accuracy." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Compared to NT, ASD participants presented with widespread reductions in CD, generally indicating shorter average connection length and thus suggesting reduced long-range connectivity but increased short-range connections." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1186/s13229-024-00616-2> ;
            slr:claim_label "Main finding: ASD shows widespread connectivity-distance reductions, implying relatively reduced long-range and increased short-range connectivity." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "We use a stratified 10-fold cross-validation strategy." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/s12559-023-10224-6> ;
            slr:claim_label "Model evaluated with stratified 10-fold cross-validation." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.6"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The preprocessing was done using the Conﬁgurable Pipeline for the Analysis of Connectomes (C-PAC, (12). We followed a preprocessing strategy adopted by the Preprocessed Connectome Project initiative3. This will allow others to replicate and extend the ﬁndings in this paper." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2020.00440> ;
            slr:claim_label "Preprocessing used C-PAC following a Preprocessed Connectomes Project strategy, chosen explicitly to enable replication." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "We esti- mated the NeuroHarmonize model parameters on the entire cohort of control subjects, by specifying the age as a covariate, whose effect is to be preserved during the harmonization process. Finally, we applied the esti- mated model on the entire sample of subjects with ASD and TD controls." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1186/s40708-023-00217-4> ;
            slr:claim_label "NeuroHarmonize (ComBat-based) site harmonization parameters were estimated on the entire cohort (controls, then applied to all subjects) rather than within CV folds." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The IMPAC fMRI and sMRI were processed using the fconn1000 ­pipeline41. For the fMRI connectivity features, the TSE connectivity metric was fit on either the training data alone (IMPAC models) or the entire IMPAC dataset (ABIDE 1 and 2 datasets), and the TSE values per-ROI timeseries for the ABIDE dataset were calculated." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-022-06459-2> ;
            slr:claim_label "Processing pipeline (fconn1000) and feature-embedding (TSE) procedure for IMPAC and ABIDE connectivity features." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """For the edge weights of the population graph
on the ABIDE datset, we incorporate the subject’s gender, age
and acquisition site as as phenotypic measures.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/s12559-023-10224-6> ;
            slr:claim_label "Site, age and gender are used as phenotypic edge-weight features in the population graph used for node classification." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """Thus, to
minimize the site eﬀect in our analysis, we included it as a
covariate in group-level statistics as described in the section 2.3.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnsys.2018.00074> ;
            slr:claim_label "Site was included as a covariate in group-level statistics to minimize the multicentric site effect." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "it is parcellated using the Harvard-Oxford (HO) atlas. After downloading the pre-processed data, 110 ROIs are acquired using the HO atlas." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1109/tmi.2023.3337362> ;
            slr:claim_label "Parcellation: Harvard-Oxford atlas, 110 ROIs." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """To further demonstrate the robustness and replicability of our findings we conducted the full 
FC mapping and analysis of group differences separately in the LEAP and 
ABIDE 1&2 data.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biopsych.2022.12.018> ;
            slr:claim_label "Findings were replicated by repeating the full analysis separately within LEAP and within the combined ABIDE I/II data." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.75"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """The analysis of the results reveals the inﬂuence of the frontal and temporal
lobes in the diagnosis of the disorder.
This
ﬁnding is consistent with
previous reports of the literature of neuroscience.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.media.2021.101986> ;
            slr:claim_label "Predictive markers implicate frontal and temporal lobe regions in ASD classification, consistent with prior neuroscience literature." ;
