            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/srep37422> ;
            slr:claim_label "Seven ABIDE I sites met inclusion criteria: UM_1, UM_2, USM, NYU, UCLA_1, OLIN, PITT." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.7"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The results show that the proposed architecture 3DCNN C-LSTM outperforms other models on single site experiments by achieving mean test accuracies and F1 scores of 0.77 and 0.78 respectively for the NYU site and 0.71 and 0.7 on the UM site." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-32695-1_11> ;
            slr:claim_label "3DCNN C-LSTM: NYU accuracy 0.77/F1 0.78; UM accuracy 0.71/F1 0.70." ;
            slr:relevance_score "1.0"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """The final 
ABIDE I and II dataset of N = 1019 included N = 82 
females with autism, N = 362 males with autism, N = 166 
neurotypical females (NT F), and N = 409 neurotypical 
males (NT M), aggregated across 13 sites.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1186/s13229-021-00415-z> ;
            slr:claim_label "The ABIDE I+II discovery sample totalled N=1019 (82 F ASD, 362 M ASD, 166 NT F, 409 NT M) across 13 sites." ;
            slr:relevance_score "1.0"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """After preprocessing and quality control, the ﬁnal dataset consists
of 1,035 samples distributed as follows: 623 samples for the
training set, 308 samples for the validation set, and 104 samples
for the test set.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/frai.2025.1594372> ;
            slr:claim_label "After QC, 1,035 subjects were split into a single train/validation/test partition (623/308/104), with no cross-validation or site handling described." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The replication dataset consisted of 584 resting-state fMRI datasets from nine sites contributing to the ‘ABIDE’ release (Di Martino et al., 2013). In this sample, all participants with ASD (278) had a clinician’s DSM-IV-TR diagnosis of ASD, which was corroborated by the Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule (ADOS) and the Autism Diagnostic Interview-Revised (Lord et al., 1994, 1999) for all sites except one." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1093/scan/nst156> ;
            slr:claim_label "The ABIDE replication sample comprised 584 resting-state datasets from nine ABIDE sites, with ASD diagnosis corroborated by ADOS/ADI-R at all but one site." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "source code available at https://github.com/sk1712/gcn_metric_learning" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-66182-7_54> ;
            slr:claim_label "Source code for the method is publicly released." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.5"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "achieving an accuracy of 0.673 on the ADHD-200 holdout data and 0.643 on the ABIDE holdout data. Both of these results, obtained with the same LEFMSF framework, are the best known, over all hold-out accuracies on these datasets when only using imaging data—exceeding previously-published results by 0.012 for ADHD and 0.042 for Autism." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0194856> ;
            slr:claim_label "The combined structural+functional learner (LEFMSF) achieves 0.643 hold-out accuracy on ABIDE, the best known result using imaging data alone at the time, exceeding prior work by 0.042." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """Functional connectivity matrices are derived from three brain
atlases (AAL, CC, EZ) using Pearson correlation coeﬃcients, which
are ﬂattened into one-dimensional vectors.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/frai.2025.1594372> ;
            slr:claim_label "Features are Pearson-correlation connectivity matrices from three atlases (AAL, CC, EZ)." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The preprocessing method used in this paper is the conﬁgurable pipeline for the analysis of connectomes (CPAC)" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnagi.2022.948704> ;
            slr:claim_label "fMRI preprocessing used the CPAC pipeline." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Skipping subjects lacking ﬁlename, we downloaded 106, 175, 72, 71 subjects from UM1, NYU, USM, UCLA1 separately. HO parcellated each brain into 111 ROIs. Since some sub- jects did not contain complete ROIs, we removed the incom- plete data, resulting in 88, 167, 52, 63 subjects for UM1, NYU, USM, UCLA1 separately." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.media.2020.101765> ;
            slr:claim_label "After removing subjects with incomplete ROI data, the analysed sample was 88 (UM1), 167 (NYU), 52 (USM), 63 (UCLA1) subjects." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The rs-fMRI scans selected from ABIDE I and ABIDE II cohorts were processed with the Configurable Pipe- line for the Analysis of Connectomes (C-PAC) [20]" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1186/s40708-023-00217-4> ;
            slr:claim_label "rs-fMRI preprocessed with C-PAC; structural data with Freesurfer." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
