            slr:claim_label "fMRI preprocessing used C-PAC v1.8.0." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "we conducted mega- and meta-analyses of resting-state functional magnetic resonance imaging data of 939 participants (440 ASD patients and 499 healthy controls, all males) from 18 independent sites, selected from the ABIDE (Autism Brain Imaging Data Exchange) dataset." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biopsych.2021.12.004> ;
            slr:claim_label "Study mega/meta-analyzed rsfMRI connectome dynamics in 939 ABIDE participants (440 ASD, 499 HC) from 18 sites." ;
            slr:relevance_score "1.0"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """a new multi-site open data resource containing 1,044 independent datasets (ASD N = 487;
Controls N = 557)""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2017.10> ;
            slr:claim_label "ABIDE II aggregates 1,044 datasets: 487 ASD and 557 controls." ;
            slr:relevance_score "1.0"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """With this approach, even with a simple 3-layer neural network, we are able to achieve a
classiﬁcation accuracy of 69.2% on the
ABIDE data set.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-32248-9_82> ;
            slr:claim_label "The hybrid topological+correlation 3-layer neural network achieved 69.2% classification accuracy." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "we used the same 871 samples from the ABIDE 1 data set [23], [24], [25]. Of the 871 subjects, 403 patients were ASD and 468 were TC patients." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.35377/saucis.04.01.879735> ;
            slr:claim_label "Cohort was a commonly-used 871-subject ABIDE I subset: 403 ASD, 468 TC." ;
            slr:relevance_score "1.0"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "First, we implemented a 10-fold cross-validation scheme for ABIDE-I to be consistent with previously reported classiﬁcation re- sults [1, 18]. Second, we trained each model on all of ABIDE-I and computed test performance on an independent held-out set from ABIDE-II. This is used for assessing the generalization behavior of diﬀerent classiﬁers. We report accu- racy and the receiver operating curves (ROC), along with corresponding area under the curves (AUC) for each of these scenarios." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-00889-5_16> ;
            slr:claim_label "Evaluation used 10-fold CV on ABIDE-I plus an independent held-out test on ABIDE-II, reporting accuracy and AUC." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """The ABIDE-I dataset is 
composed of 1112 resting-state functional magnetic resonance 
imaging (rs-fMRI) datasets. Among these, 573 datasets belong 
to typically developing persons, while 539 datasets belong to 
individuals with autism. On the other hand, the ABIDE-II 
dataset consists of 1014 resting-state functional magnetic 
resonance imaging (rs-fMRI) datasets. Out of these, 521 
datasets are from individuals with autism, and 593 datasets are 
from typically developing control individuals.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1109/tce.2023.3328479> ;
            slr:claim_label "ABIDE-I has 1112 datasets (573 TC, 539 ASD); ABIDE-II has 1014 (should be 1114 per abstract) with 521 ASD and 593 control datasets." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The ABIDE data is publicly available. We have uploaded to ABIDE the indexes of the participants included in the current study." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnint.2020.00023> ;
            slr:claim_label "Participant indices for this study were uploaded to ABIDE, enabling cohort reconstruction." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.6"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """The DPARSF is a MATLAB toolbox for fMRI data pre-
processing and analysing [17].""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.30880/ijie.2021.13.05.006> ;
            slr:claim_label "Preprocessing pipeline was DPARSF." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.7"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "fMRI image could be divided into 90 regions based on the Automatic Anatomical Labeling (AAL) (Tzourio-Mazoyer et al., 2002) atlas. We make these regions as the nodes of brain network, so there are 90 nodes. An average of the time series of a region’s all voxels can be used to capture the mean time series of this region (Khazaee et al., 2016). The average time series of every two brain regions can be employed to calculate the Pearson correlation coeﬃcient which is made as the link of the brain network (Khazaee et al., 2015), so there are 4,005 (90∗89/2) weighted edges." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fgene.2018.00018> ;
            slr:claim_label "The brain was parcellated into 90 regions using the AAL atlas, yielding 4,005 pairwise connectivity edges." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The overall best performing model was the MM-ensemble, which achieved balanced accuracy of 64% and F1 score of 66%, averaged over the ﬁve-folds of the CV procedure. With the leave- site-out CV procedure the performance of the MM-ensemble dropped to an average balanced accuracy of mean 56% and F1 score of 59%, suggesting that this model does not do well in generalizing to new sites." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2020.00440> ;
            slr:claim_label "The best model (MM-ensemble) reached 64% balanced accuracy / 66% F1 under 5-fold CV, dropping to 56% balanced accuracy / 59% F1 under leave-site-out CV." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """We used resting state fMRI data of 458 subjects with ASD and
517 TDCs (see Table 1 for additional demographic information)
among 1112 datasets from the ABIDE datasets""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2016.00191> ;
            slr:claim_label "458 ASD and 517 TDC subjects were selected from 1112 ABIDE datasets." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The extracted features are trained  using two classifiers: support vector machine (SVM) and K-nearest neighbours (KNN). The best prediction results  are 85.9% accuracy achieved by extracted the features from DenseNet201 network and classified these features by  KNN classifier." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.30880/ijie.2021.13.05.006> ;
            slr:claim_label "Best classification result: 85.9% accuracy using DenseNet201-extracted features with a KNN classifier." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """GCN [15]
64.63
72.23
64.63
86.33
64.63
26.64
30.16""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/s12559-023-10224-6> ;
            slr:claim_label "Baseline GCN achieved 64.63% accuracy / 72.23% AUC on ABIDE." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.6"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Table 2 shows the average classification performances obtained by 10-fold cross-validation tests. When the classification results are examined, it is seen that the highest performance value is provided by RNN with 74.74%." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.35377/saucis.04.01.879735> ;
            slr:claim_label "RNN was the best-performing model at 74.74% accuracy." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "These tuned models achieved AUROC as high as 93.2% on ABIDE-I and 90.5% on ABIDE-II, roughly a 4–9 basis point increase in performance relative to models without any adaptation." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-022-06459-2> ;
            slr:claim_label "Supervised domain adaptation raised AUROC to 93.2% on ABIDE-I and 90.5% on ABIDE-II." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """inhibition revolved around edges in the somato-motor, visual and cerebellar 
7 
networks and was more posterior, while shifting appeared more focused on edges around the 
8 
frontoparietal and dorsal attention networks and was more anterior.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dcn.2019.100747> ;
            slr:claim_label "Inhibition and shifting predictive networks involved distinct brain network sets (posterior somato-motor/visual/cerebellar vs anterior frontoparietal/dorsal attention)." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.7"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """We preprocessed the imaging data using the Athena pipeline
(www.nitrc.org/plugins/mwiki/index.php/neurobureau:Athena
Pipeline).
The
pipeline
focused
on
providing
systematic
processing of fMRI data, including the following main steps:
exclusion of the ﬁrst four scans; slice timing correction;""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnsys.2018.00074> ;
            slr:claim_label "Imaging data were preprocessed using the Athena pipeline." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """MGRL (Ours)
0.795 ± 0.068
0.809 ± 0.146
0.823 ± 0.103
0.802 ± 0.075
0.886 ± 0.062""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fninf.2021.802305> ;
            slr:claim_label "MGRL main NYU result: accuracy 0.795, recall 0.809, precision 0.823, F1 0.802, AUC 0.886." ;
            slr:relevance_score "1.0"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """where ABIDE-I and 
ABIDE-II consists of 1112 rs- fMRI datasets from 573 typical 
control (TC) and 539 autism individuals, and 1114 rs-fMRI from 
521 autism and 593 typical control individuals respectively, 
which were collected from 17 different sites.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1109/tce.2023.3328479> ;
            slr:claim_label "ABIDE-I and ABIDE-II together comprise 1112 and 1114 rs-fMRI datasets respectively, from 17 different sites." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Site bias was corrected among diﬀerent sites similar to an approach described previously by an ABIDE study (Heinsfeld et al., 2018). Speciﬁcally, a multiple regression analysis was conducted to control for potentially confounding variables (site, age, gender, and handedness). These variables were regressed from FC weights across connections among ROIs. When adjusting for the confounding factors, our regression model is: y = β0 + β1x1 + β2x2 + β3x3 + β4x4 + ε where y is the vector of FC weights, x1 to x4 represent the four explanatory variables, site, age, gender, and handedness. βi is the intercept and the corresponding regression coeﬃcients. ε is the residual vector. Using ordinary least squares (OLS) estimation, βi was estimated. Then, these cofounding variables were regressed out from the FC weights." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2018.00491> ;
            slr:claim_label "Site, age, gender and handedness were regressed out of FC weights via OLS multiple regression to correct for site bias." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """The results suggest that the levels of random involuntary
motor noise are elevated in autism across age groups.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnint.2020.00023> ;
            slr:claim_label "Main finding: random involuntary motor noise (head micro-motion) is elevated in ASD relative to TD across age groups." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """In
this validation analysis, three out of ﬁve cortical ROIs, namely,
the right fusiform gyrus [β
=
−0.028, t-value = −2.193,
p = 0.047 —t-test (GLM)], the right superior temporal gyrus
[β = −0.044, t-value = −3.495, p = 0.002 —t-test (GLM)],
and the left middle temporal gyrus [β
=
−0.033, t-value
= −2.583, p = 0.025—t-test (GLM)], conﬁrmed the reduced
functional connectivity in the ASD group""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnsys.2018.00074> ;
            slr:claim_label "In the ABIDE II validation sample, 3 of 5 ROIs (right fusiform gyrus, right superior temporal gyrus, left middle temporal gyrus) replicated the reduced connectivity finding." ;
            slr:relevance_score "1.0"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Using data  8  from two sites of the ABIDE II dataset comprising 276 children with and without ASD (8-13 years),  9  we identified functional brain networks whose FC predicted individual differences in two, of three,  10  behavioral regu" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dcn.2019.100747> ;
            slr:claim_label "Final cohort: 276 children (ASD and TD) aged 8-13 from two ABIDE II sites." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """Although Di Martino et al. [11] released the ABIDE I dataset with 1,112 samples, prepro-
cessing and quality control reduced this number to 1,035""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.compbiomed.2024.109083> ;
            slr:claim_label "The released ABIDE I dataset of 1,112 samples was reduced to 1,035 after preprocessing and quality control." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The GAT2 model achieved the best results in accuracy, sensitivity, F1 score, and MCC  indicators using fivefold cross-validation, with the accuracy of 68.02%, sensitivity of  74.06%, F1 score of 69.31%, and MCC of 0.3426." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1186/s12859-021-04295-1> ;
            slr:claim_label "Main predictive performance: GAT2 best model, accuracy 68.02%, sensitivity 74.06%, F1 69.31%, MCC 0.3426." ;
            slr:relevance_score "1.0"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "from 17 international sites2. The ROIs fMRI series of all sites are downloaded from the pre-processed ABIDE dataset with a configurable pipeline for the analysis of connectomes (CPAC), band-pass filter- ing (0.01 −0.1Hz), and no global signal regression" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1109/tmi.2023.3337362> ;
            slr:claim_label "Preprocessing pipeline: CPAC, band-pass filtered, no global signal regression, across 17 sites." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """In the ABIDE cohort, group-mean FD was
0.124 for ASD and 0.123 for TD (two sample t-test p =
0.8679).""" ] ;
