            slr:relevance_score "0.5"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """our work has two main limitations: one is that the proposed
model still cannot explain the pathogenesis of the detected
abnormal brain connections; the other is that the dataset
used in the current study is relatively small.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1109/tpami.2024.3442811> ;
            slr:claim_label "Authors note interpretability and small dataset size as limitations." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.4"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Table 3. Demographics of IMPAC participants, ABIDE I participants, and ABIDE II participants. Errors shown are standard deviations. IMPAC ABIDE I ABIDE II Female % 50 15 20 ASD % 46 48 52 Age (years) 17 ± 9.6 17 ± 8.1 17 ± 11 Total participants 915 1045 761" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-022-06459-2> ;
            slr:claim_label "Demographic breakdown (sex %, ASD %, age, total N) for the IMPAC, ABIDE I and ABIDE II analysed samples." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """In this study, we consider the ABIDE I preprocessed dataset (Di Martino
et al., 2014; Craddock et al., 2013). It includes BOLD time-series extracted
from rs-fMRI through a preprocessing pipeline which is fully detailed on the web
platforms related to the ABIDE collection""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.media.2021.101986> ;
            slr:claim_label "Uses the ABIDE I Preprocessed Connectomes Project dataset of rs-fMRI BOLD time series." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """The task is to diagnose a patient as being of two classes
– Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD) or Typical Control (TC).""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1109/icassp.2019.8683547> ;
            slr:claim_label "Main claim is diagnostic classification of ASD vs typical control." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Craddock 200 (CC200) functional parcellation (Craddock et al., 2012)" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fncom.2021.654315> ;
            slr:claim_label "Functional parcellation used the Craddock 200 (CC200) atlas." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """our developed
MHOA based on the SSDAE model has accuracy 66.35%, 70.19%,
and 83.82% for EZ, AAL, and CC, respectively.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/frai.2025.1594372> ;
            slr:claim_label "Per-atlas accuracy: EZ 66.35%, AAL 70.19%, CC 83.82%." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """R-fMRI image pre-processing 
steps included: slice time correction, 24 motion param-
eters regression [57], component-based noise reduction 
(CompCor) [58], removal of linear and quadratic trends, 
and band-pass filtering (0.01–0.1 Hz, for all metrics but 
fALFF).""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1186/s13229-021-00415-z> ;
            slr:claim_label "R-fMRI preprocessing included slice-time correction, 24-motion-parameter regression, CompCor noise reduction, detrending, and band-pass filtering; five metrics examined: PCC-iFC, VMHC, ReHo, DC, fALFF." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The identified subtype-specific patterns are only predictive for ASD symptoms manifested in the corresponding subtypes, but not the other subtypes." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1186/s13229-020-00397-4> ;
            slr:claim_label "Subtype-specific brain patterns predict only the corresponding subtype's symptoms, not other subtypes." ;
            slr:relevance_score "1.0"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The ABIDE dataset consists of 1111 scans, taken from 17 sites consisting of 573 healthy controls and 538 patients with autism. To evaluate each learning model, we use 800 subjects (70%) for model training and 311 subjects (30%) for hold-out testing. We use the same case/control ratio (0.5157) for both training and test set." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0194856> ;
            slr:claim_label "ABIDE: 1111 scans from 17 sites (573 HC, 538 ASD), split 800 (70%) training / 311 (30%) hold-out test, preserving the case:control ratio in both sets." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "On the combined site data across 17 sites, we achieved the maximum 10-fold accuracy of 82% and for the individual site-wise data, based on 5-fold accuracy, our results outperformed other state of the art methods in 13 out of the total 17 site-wise comparisons." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3390/brainsci10100754> ;
            slr:claim_label "Main finding: 82% maximum 10-fold accuracy on the combined 17-site dataset, outperforming prior methods in 13/17 individual sites." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """The SN-dDMN and SN-LCEN pairs showed
increased connectivity strength in ASD, and hypo-connectivity
was observed in the PCUN-dDMN pair of ASD.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnhum.2021.687288> ;
            slr:claim_label "ASD showed hyperconnectivity between salience network (SN) and dorsal DMN, and between SN and left central executive network, and hypoconnectivity between precuneus and dorsal DMN." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "All experiments were conducted with a 10-fold cross-validation to divide the dataset into training and test sets, with 10% of the training set randomly selected as the validation set. Ultimately, the training, validation, and test sets were non-overlapping." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41398-024-02972-2> ;
            slr:claim_label "Train/validation/test sets were kept non-overlapping within the 10-fold CV scheme." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """ABIDE 
PANDA 
7.25 × 102 
0.64 
technician-dependent 
DGCL 
2.19 × 100 
0.71 
highly-automated""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1109/tpami.2024.3442811> ;
            slr:claim_label "On ABIDE, the proposed DGCL brain-network construction had higher reliability (ICC 0.71) and lower construction time than the PANDA baseline (ICC 0.64)." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.6"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """The current ABIDE II dataset encompasses 17 collections of unique independent datasets (i.e., from
individuals whose data were not previously shared in ABIDE I) yielding 487 datasets classiﬁed as ASD
and 557 as controls (Fig. 1a, Table 1). These represent previously collected datasets across 16 sites,
including nine charter ABIDE I institutions and seven new members""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2017.10> ;
            slr:claim_label "ABIDE II comprises 17 collections across 16 sites (9 ABIDE I charter sites plus 7 new sites)." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "A ﬁnal dataset of 871 subjects, including 403 ASD patients and 468 TCs, was obtained by removing the samples with incomplete brain coverage, high motion peaks, ghosting and other scanner artifacts." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnagi.2022.948704> ;
            slr:claim_label "Final analysed sample after QC was 871 subjects (403 ASD/468 TC), excluding incomplete coverage, high motion peaks, ghosting and other artifacts." ;
            slr:relevance_score "1.0"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """The independent
components were derived using Group-ICA, and further inspected to identify eight well deﬁned brain function networks (BFNs). (B) The selected BFNs were used to
extract subject-speciﬁc spatial maps using dual regression.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnhum.2021.687288> ;
            slr:claim_label "Eight brain functional networks were derived via group-ICA and subject-specific maps via dual regression, used as 3-D CNN input." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.75"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "We preprocessed the data with the Conﬁgurable Pipeline for the Analysis of Connectomes (C-PAC) and the fMRI volumes are downsampled to 4 mm in MNI." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-32695-1_11> ;
            slr:claim_label "Preprocessing pipeline is C-PAC with 4mm MNI downsampling; no ROI atlas used (raw 4D volumes)." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "We selected only ASD participants from the ABIDE database since diagnostic scores were  not available for controls. We selected the same 5 datasets used in (1), that is sites with  codes: 'CALTECH' (n=19), 'CMU' (n=14), 'PITT' (n=30), 'UM_1' (n=55), 'UM_2' (n=13) for  a total of 131 ASD participants." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1002/hbm.23084> ;
            slr:claim_label "ABIDE subset drawn from 5 sites (CALTECH, CMU, PITT, UM_1, UM_2), 131 ASD participants before further restriction; no ABIDE controls used because diagnostic scores were unavailable for them." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
