            slr:claim_label "Evaluation used 5-fold stratified cross-validation." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The rs- fMRI data were processed using Connectome Computation System (Xu et al., 2015) pipeline, which includes slice timing correction, motion realignment, and intensity normalization. Nuisance variable regression (Fox et al., 2005; Lund et al., 2005) was implemented through band-pass ﬁltering and global signal regression strategies to clean confounding variations introduced by heartbeats and respirations, head motion, and low frequency scanner drifts. Furthermore, boundary-based rigid body and FMRIB’s linear & nonlinear image registration tools (Andersson et al., 2008; Ratziu et al., 2008) were used to register functional to anatomical images. Then, both functional and anatomical images were normalized to a standard template space, the Automated Anatomical Labeling atlas (Tzourio-Mazoyer et al., 2002)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2018.00491> ;
            slr:claim_label "Data were preprocessed with the Connectome Computation System pipeline and parcellated with the AAL atlas into a 90x90 functional connectivity matrix." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "After the removal of subjects with image artifacts, high head movement, or poor MNI152 coregistration, we analyzed the data from the remaining 710 ASD (79% male), and 606 CTL (87% male) subjects, whose age ranges from 5 to 64 years." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-31053-5> ;
            slr:claim_label "After QC exclusions, 710 ASD and 606 CTL subjects were analysed." ;
            slr:relevance_score "1.0"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """In our experiment, we employed the 10-fold cross-
validation strategy to conduct the comparison among dif-
ferent models.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neunet.2025.107450> ;
            slr:claim_label "Evaluation used pooled 10-fold cross-validation (no leave-site-out scheme described)." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Subjects with ASD (n = 229) and the corresponding TDCs (n = 126) were selected from the ABIDE II [29, 30], which is hosted by the 1000 Functional Connectome Project/International Neuroimaging Data-sharing Ini- tiative (INDI) from multiple international sites (9 sites, Additional file 1: Table S1)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1186/s13229-020-00397-4> ;
            slr:claim_label "ABIDE II discovery sample: 229 ASD, 126 TDC from 9 sites." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """Validation on two datasets, ADNI and ABIDE, demonstrates that DGCL surpasses traditional methods and other deep
learning models in predicting disease development stages.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1109/tpami.2024.3442811> ;
            slr:claim_label "The proposed diffusion-based graph contrastive learning model is validated on both ADNI and ABIDE for disease classification." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.7"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """TABLE 9 | Peak similarity (highlighted), corresponding number of features, and number of clusters obtained using SFR, SFS, and GA with different clustering methods for
ASD dataset.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fams.2018.00025> ;
            slr:claim_label "Table 9 reports peak similarity between clinical-diagnostic, phenotypic and connectivity-based clusters for ASD across feature-selection and clustering methods." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.6"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Both datasets are available online publicly. The ADHD-200 dataset is available at: http://fcon_1000.projects.nitrc.org/ indi/adhd200/ The ABIDE dataset is available at: (http://fcon_1000.projects.nitrc.org/indi/abide/)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0194856> ;
            slr:claim_label "Both the ADHD-200 and ABIDE datasets used are publicly available online." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.6"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """Participants with ASD were diagnosed based on an in-person interview administered by
