        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "TABLE 2 | Demographic data of the healthy and autism spectrum disorder (ASD) subjects across seven data sites ordered by decreasing sample size. Site Class Target task sample size Age (years) Gender (male%) Handedness (right%)* Mean full-scale IQ* Ofﬂine learning sample size UM ASD 48 13.8 ± 2 81.30 75 107.6 ± 17.3 411 Healthy 65 15 ± 3.7 75.40 83.10 109 ± 9.5 UCLA ASD 36 13.3 ± 3 94.40 88.90 102.4 ± 12.8 437 Healthy 39 13.2 ± 1.8 84.60 92.30 106.4 ± 10.4 USM ASD 38 24.6 ± 9 100 92.10 99.7 ± 17.3 453 Healthy 23 22.3 ± 7.9 100 95.70 115.5 ± 15.6 LEUVEN ASD 27 18 ± 5 92.60 88.90 109.4 ± 13.1 442 Healthy 34 18.2 ± 5.1 85.30 85.30 114.8 ± 12.9 All ± values are mean ± SD. *Results were calculated after removing missing data. Number of IQ missing value: UM, ASD-1, Healthy-3; UCLA, ASD-0, Healthy-0; USM, ASD-0, Healthy-0; LEUVEN, ASD-13, Healthy-19" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2018.00491> ;
            slr:claim_label "Per-site ASD/healthy sample sizes and demographics across the four target sites and the offline-learning pool from the remaining sites." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """We took the so far best performing classifier – the support 
vector machine – and applied it to the data set after this stand-
ardization was performed. The resulting classification accuracy 
increased from 63 to 68%.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2016.00177> ;
            slr:claim_label "Per-site z-standardization (train-only mean/SD) improved the best classifier's (SVM) accuracy from 63% to 68%." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Previous studies have reported cross- validated classiﬁcation accuracies up to 67% on ABIDE-I, the ﬁrst phase of the ABIDE study [1]. The proposed CNN approach improves this accuracy to above 73%." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-00889-5_16> ;
            slr:claim_label "The proposed 3D-CNN improves cross-validated ABIDE-I accuracy from a prior benchmark of 67% to above 73%." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """The study 
included resting-state fMRI and clinical data from the LEAP and the ABIDE I and II initiatives, 
of 1824 (796 with autism) participants with age range 5-58 years.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biopsych.2022.12.018> ;
            slr:claim_label "Mega-analysis combines EU-AIMS LEAP with ABIDE I and ABIDE II for a total of 1824 participants (796 autism)." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Diagnosis was established with the Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule (ADOS) [39], the Autism Diagnostic Interview Revised (ADI-R) [40] as well as clini- cal consensus." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0190081> ;
            slr:claim_label "Diagnosis established via ADOS, ADI-R and clinical consensus." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.6"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "the resulting hold-out accuracy for ADHD was 0.6491 (baseline 0.5497) and was 0.6233 for ABIDE (baseline 0.5157). The specificity, sensitivity and Jstat for ADHD (resp., ABIDE) are 0.8191, 0.4416 and 0.2607 (respectively, 0.6768, 0.5533 and 0.2301). To our knowl- edge, our holdout accuracies achieved on ADHD-200 test data and the ABIDE test data are the best known when only using fMRI scans." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0194856> ;
            slr:claim_label "Hold-out accuracy was 0.6233 for ABIDE (baseline 0.5157), described as the best known result using fMRI scans alone." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "We chose to cut off the minimum scan duration to 100-time points, which led us to include 96% of the whole ABIDE I+II dataset (N=2,085, N(ASD) =993), the vast majority of which (95%) with a minimum acquisition time of 4 min." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2020.00440> ;
            slr:claim_label "A minimum scan-duration cutoff of 100 time points retained 96% of ABIDE I+II (N=2,085, N(ASD)=993)." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "to avoid signiﬁcant inter-site heterogeneity, we mainly used rs-fMRI data from the NYU site. While ABIDE contains data from 21 sites, as a future work, we will evaluate the proposed method on all sites in ABIDE and design smart techniques to reduce inter-site data heterogeneity." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fninf.2021.802305> ;
            slr:claim_label "Authors deliberately restricted to single sites (NYU/UM) to avoid inter-site heterogeneity; no multi-site/leave-site-out evaluation performed." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.7"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """a leave-site out cross-validation scheme was performed: 
each training set was composed by all the sites except one, that 
was left out for validation.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2019.00620> ;
            slr:claim_label "Classification used a leave-one-site-out cross-validation scheme." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """To 
assess FC group differences, a general linear model was fitted to each edge, including 
diagnosis, age, sex, and mean framewise displacement (FD) as covariates.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biopsych.2022.12.018> ;
            slr:claim_label "Group differences were assessed with a GLM per edge including diagnosis, age, sex and mean FD as covariates, analysed with the Network Based Statistic." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Resting-state fMRI data from 850 subjects in ABIDE I with an ASD DSM-IV-TR diagnosis (n = 355) and the corresponding HCs (n = 495) from the same sites were used in this study" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fncom.2021.762781> ;
            slr:claim_label "Analysed ABIDE I cohort: 355 ASD, 495 HC (850 total)." ;
            slr:relevance_score "1.0"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "a total of 14 children with ASD and 28 TC children were excluded, and the final sample included 42 children with ASD and 127 TC children." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2022.987248> ;
            slr:claim_label "14 ASD and 28 TC children were excluded (poor normalization, excessive motion, non-convergence of spDCM), leaving 42 ASD/127 TC." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """Frames that exhibited an FD of over 0.5 mm were
censored from the timeseries, as well as one before and
two after the offending frame.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41398-021-01221-0> ;
            slr:claim_label "Frames with FD over 0.5 mm (plus one before and two after) were censored (scrubbed) from the timeseries." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """The minimum MSE computed from a 10-fold cross validation
was 11.4 ± 7.2% of c1 variance, and was observed for α = 0.15.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2018.00869> ;
            slr:claim_label "Elastic-net model of FC from RSN entropy was fit with 10-fold cross-validation." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.6"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """The proposed HCAN method achieves an average ACC of 82.9%, 
SEN of 76.7%, SPE of 86.6% and AUC of 84.6%.""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1186/s12859-023-05495-7> ;
            slr:claim_label "10-fold CV performance: ACC 82.9%, sensitivity 76.7%, specificity 86.6%, AUC 84.6%." ;
            slr:relevance_score "1.0"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "A total of 964 subjects met all inclusion criteria (517 typically developing subjects and 447 subjects with autism from 16 sites)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnhum.2013.00599> ;
            slr:claim_label "Analysed cohort: 964 ABIDE I participants (447 autism, 517 typically developing) from 16 sites after applying inclusion criteria." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "the accuracy of the random SVM cluster is as high as 96.15%. This is suﬃcient to show that the performance of the random SVM cluster is much better than a single SVM." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fgene.2018.00018> ;
            slr:claim_label "The random SVM cluster achieved 96.15% accuracy, much higher than a single SVM." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "compared to HCs, we found that fractional occupancies of HMM states 4, 8, 9, and 10 for ASD subjects were signiﬁcantly decreased" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnhum.2022.774921> ;
            slr:claim_label "ASD subjects showed significantly decreased fractional occupancy in HMM brain states 4, 8, 9 and 10 relative to controls." ;
            slr:relevance_score "1.0"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "For the multi-site experiment we used ABIDE-I with 19 sites and 1100 subjects." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-32695-1_11> ;
            slr:claim_label "Multi-site cohort: 19 ABIDE-I sites, 1100 subjects." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value """We observed that an imbalance in intra- and inter-network FC across 11 RSNs in ASD individuals (p = 0.002) corresponds to a weakened relationship with RSN
temporal entropy (p = 0.02).""" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2018.00869> ;
            slr:claim_label "Main finding: FC imbalance across 11 RSNs in ASD corresponds to a weaker FC-entropy relationship than in controls." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Using automated anatomical labeling (AAL), we then used the ﬁrst 90 regions of interest (ROIs) as nodes" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2017.00125> ;
            slr:claim_label "AAL atlas, first 90 ROIs used as network nodes." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Speciﬁcally, the 507 subjects included 209 subjects with ASD and 298 well-matched health controls across 14 sites from the Autism Brain Imaging Data Exchange (ABIDE)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnhum.2022.774921> ;
            slr:claim_label "Cohort: 507 male subjects (209 ASD, 298 controls) from 14 ABIDE sites." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ] ;
