                    slr:judgment "unclear" ;
                    slr:supporting_quote "10-fold cross-validation is used and overfitting-control steps are described (We minimized the risk of overﬁtting by using three limiting approaches. First, the simplest kernel (linear) was used for the SVM. Second, only 10 features were used to learn to classify between 104 subjects. Finally, using 10-fold cross validation ensured the model is only evaluated on data points that it has not experienced before.), but the text does not state whether the sequential feature selection step (reducing 817 features to 10) was nested within each CV fold or performed once on the full dataset before cross-validation, and sites are pooled within each age group with no site covariate or harmonisation." ],
