            slr:source_id "S-056" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1207 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE II, KKI site only: 211 children originally (56 ASD/155 TC, ages 8-13), 14 ASD and 28 TC excluded for poor normalization/excessive motion/spDCM non-convergence, final n=42 ASD/127 TC. | quote: \"a total of 14 children with ASD and 28 TC children were excluded, and the ﬁnal sample included 42 children with ASD and 127 TC children.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-082" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1226 ;
            slr:answer_text "predictive — ABIDE I only, raw N=1112 reduced to 1,035 after preprocessing/QC (505 ASD, 530 TC); no explicit FD/motion threshold given in the extracted main text (QC described generically as reducing N to 1035, consistent with prior studies) | quote: \"Although Di Martino et al. [11] released the ABIDE I dataset with 1,112 samples, prepro- cessing and quality control reduced this number to 1,035\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-014" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1208 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE-I single-site cohorts (NYU: 184 subjects; UM: 110 subjects) and a multi-site cohort (19 sites, 1100 subjects); no explicit motion/QC exclusion rule stated. | quote: \"For single sites experiments, we use the NYU and UM sites from ABIDE-I. Those provide the highest number of balanced (ASD/typically developing (TD)) subjects with 184 and 110 subjects respectively.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-058" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1246 ;
            slr:answer_text """ABIDE-I, 848 of the 1112 subjects across 17 sites (396 ASD, 452 HC); no explicit numeric exclusion/QC rule given for the subset selection. | quote: "we utilized rs-fMRI data
from 848 subjects, including 396 patients with ASD and 452
health controls (HCs).\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-090" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1244 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE II (9 sites, discovery: ASD n=229 [Asperger's 79, PDD-NOS 58, Autistic 92], TDC n=126) and ABIDE I (17 sites, n=400, replication), males only, age<35 | quote: \"Subjects with ASD (n = 229) and the corresponding TDCs (n = 126) were selected from the ABIDE II [29, 30], which is hosted by the 1000 Functional Connectome Project/International Neuroimaging Data-sharing Ini- tiative (INDI) from multiple international sites (9 sites, Additional file 1: Table S1).\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-009" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1219 ;
            slr:answer_text """predictive | ABIDE release, N, sites and exclusion/QC rule are not reported in the available text; only the autism dataset's existence and ASD-vs-HC classification results are described. | quote: "And the largest dataset for autism research comes
from Autism Brain Imaging Data Exchange (ABIDE) [11].\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-049" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1239 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE I (ABIDE preprocessed), 539 ASD and 573 controls (1112 total); no explicit numeric QC/motion exclusion rule described beyond use of the ABIDE-preprocessed release | quote: \"The 539 subjects with ASD and the 573 controls were split 70/15/15 into training, validation and test sets.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-063" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1256 ;
            slr:answer_text "predictive, external validation only — all ABIDE I/II sites included, restricted to subjects with a paired same-visit sMRI+rsfMRI scan: 1045 ABIDE I and 761 ABIDE II subjects (Table 3: ASD% 48 and 52 respectively; exact integer N by diagnosis not given). | quote: \"Participants from all sites of the ABIDE I and ABIDE II were included for external validation, provided both sMRI and rsfMRI were obtained on the same visit. The first avail- able pair of sMRI and rsfMRI scans were used per subject. 1045 subjects from ABIDE I and 761 subjects from ABIDE II met this criteria.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-010" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1233 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE II used as a replication cohort (not the primary dataset): 5 of 16 ABIDE II sites selected (GU, KKI, NYU_1, NYU_2, SDSU) with sex/FSIQ/age/handedness/behavioural-score filters, then NYU_2 and motion/normalization failures excluded, yielding 42 ASD and 88 TD boys. | quote: \"The ﬁnal replication dataset consisted of 42 boys with ASD (mean age: 10.7 ± 1.8 years, range: 7.2–14.4 years) and 88 TD boys\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-043" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1202 ;
            slr:answer_text """ABIDE I (1112, 17 sites) + ABIDE II (983, 16 sites) for biomarker derivation (2095 total, 1001 ASD/1094 TD), plus an independent local KMUH cohort (21 ASD, 23 TD) for validation; no further ABIDE QC/exclusion rule reported beyond using the full obtained datasets. | quote: "This study included 1112 ABIDE I datasets 
from 17 sites and 983 ABIDE II datasets from 16 sites.\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-091" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1229 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE I — 816 individuals across 22 sites, stratified into five age groups (5-10: 109, 10-15: 342, 15-20: 190, 20-30: 137, 30-65: 51); subjects with a consistently zero time-series were excluded; exact ASD/HC split is in a supplementary table not captured in the extracted full text. | quote: \"All Sites 109 342 190 137 51 816 Number of participants from each site for each age group as well as the overall number of participants in a site that were used for this study. Last row shows the total number of subjects in each age-range.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-033" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1260 ;
            slr:answer_text "predictive — ABIDE-I: N=1112 (539 ASD, 573 controls), 17 sites; ABIDE-II: N reported inconsistently as 1114 (abstract) / 1014 (Table II) (521 ASD, 593 controls); no explicit QC/exclusion rule beyond removing missing/broken images (938 of 1112 ABIDE-I scans used after cleaning) | quote: \"ABIDE-I and   ABIDE-II consists of 1112 rs- fMRI datasets from 573 typical   control (TC) and 539 autism individuals, and 1114 rs-fMRI from   521 autism and 593 typical control individuals respectively,   which were collected from 17 different sites.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-004" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1166 ;
            slr:answer_text "Single ABIDE I site (University of Michigan), 48 ASD and 65 TC, no significant age/sex differences; TC inclusion/exclusion per ABIDE project criteria (IQ>=85, age>=7, SCQ<10, SCAS OC<6) | quote: \"The publicly available data set comprises data from 48 people with ASD and 65 TCs, with no signiﬁcant diﬀerences in demographics between the two groups.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-078" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1230 ;
            slr:answer_text "predictive | ABIDE I, 871 of 1112 participants (403 ASD, 468 TC) from 17 sites, selected after visual QA of MRI and phenotypic information. | quote: \"Af- ter preprocessing, we selected 871 to meet quality criteria for MRI and phenotypic information.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-002" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1213 ;
            slr:answer_text "associational — ABIDE subset: 58 ASD, 51 TD, matched to primary cohort by age/sex/IQ; participants with <80% TRs retained after motion scrubbing excluded; release (I vs II) not specified, both ABIDE I and ABIDE II papers cited as the data source | quote: \"To validate our ﬁndings in a separate cohort, we iden- tiﬁed 58 ASD and 51 TD individuals from ABIDE mat- ched to the HFASD cohort by age, sex, and IQ (Table 2). The selection process is detailed in Supplemental Infor- mation.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-007" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1172 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE I+II, QC'd to 939 participants (440 ASD/499 HC) across 18 sites, males only, age<35, FIQ>70, FD<0.5mm, scan length>=5min, sites with <10 participants per group excluded | quote: \"Thus, after all selection criteria had been applied, we obtained a dataset consisting of scans from 939 participants (ASD/HC, 440/499) taken from 18 different sites\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-005" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1169 ;
            slr:answer_text "predictive — ABIDE I+II combined (\"both waves of the openly shared ABIDE initiative\"), final N=297 (151 ASD, 146 TD) from 4 sites (NYU, PITT, USM, TCD); QC: sites with >=10/group and both children+adults, acceptable T1w MRI/surface extraction/head motion; after propensity matching N=290 (145/145) | quote: \"procedures resulted in a total of 297 par- ticipants (151 ASD and 146 TD) from 4 different sites (i.e., New York University Langone Medical Center [NYU], University of Pittsburgh, School of Medicine [PITT], University of Utah, School of Medicine [USM], and Trinity Centre for Health Sciences [TCD]) in ABIDE.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-011" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1222 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE I+II — full release 1,028 ASD/1,141 TD across 29 institutions; after a minimum-scan-duration cutoff (>=100 time points), 96% was retained (N=2,085, N(ASD)=993). | quote: \"We chose to cut off the minimum scan duration to 100-time points, which led us to include 96% of the whole ABIDE I+II dataset (N=2,085, N(ASD) =993), the vast majority of which (95%) with a minimum acquisition time of 4 min.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-030" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1197 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE I, a selected subgroup of 190 subjects (102 ASD, 88 TD) from four sites (KKI, NYU, UCLA, UM), restricted to male children aged 6.5-13 years with eyes-open rs-fMRI. | quote: \"we selected a subgroup of 190 subjects (102 with ASD and 88 TD) according to the following criteria: male children (age range: 6.5–13 years); rs-fMRI data acquired with open eyes; data from the University sites that provided the largest number of scans (KKI, NYU, UCLA, UM).\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-062" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1261 ;
            slr:answer_text """associational | ABIDE I and ABIDE II combined with EU-AIMS LEAP; ABIDE I n=369 autism/481 NT, ABIDE II n=205 autism/347 NT (combined ABIDE total autism 574, NT 828); detailed exclusion rules referenced as "Supplement Section 2", not given in body text. | quote: "n 
