            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-054" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1262 ;
            slr:answer_text "Multi-site ABIDE: 85 ASD, 163 matched controls, N=248; inclusion required T1 + rs-fMRI full coverage, full-scale IQ>100, a framewise-displacement criterion, and >=7 ASD/7 control per site; individuals with >10% scrubbed frames excluded. | quote: \"Resting-state fMRI (rs-fMRI) and structural imaging data of 85 individuals with ASD and 163 matched controls from multiple sites of the ABIDE data set (Di Martino et al., 2014) were included in this study for a total of N = 248 individuals.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-094" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1241 ;
            slr:answer_text "predictive | Same ABIDE I 871-subject subset (403 ASD, 468 controls) as Abraham et al. 2017, from 20 sites. | quote: \"We select the same set of 871 subjects used by Abraham et al. (2017) that met the imaging quality and phenotypic information criteria, comprising 403 individuals with ASD and 468 healthy controls.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-019" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1177 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE I — 584 resting-state datasets (278 ASD/306 TD) from nine ABIDE sites, used as an independent replication sample; ASD diagnosis was a clinician DSM-IV-TR diagnosis corroborated by ADOS/ADI-R at all but one site; groups matched on age (and IQ within most sites). | quote: \"The replication dataset consisted of 584 resting-state fMRI datasets from nine sites contributing to the ‘ABIDE’ release (Di Martino et al., 2013). In this sample, all participants with ASD (278) had a clinician’s DSM-IV-TR diagnosis of ASD, which was corroborated by the Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule (ADOS) and the Autism Diagnostic Interview-Revised (Lord et al., 1994, 1999) for all sites except one.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-026" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1203 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE I — top four largest sites (UM1, NYU, USM, UCLA1): after excluding subjects with missing files or incomplete ROI time series, analysed N = 88 (UM1), 167 (NYU), 52 (USM), 63 (UCLA1); ASD/HC per site given in Table 1 (overall 186 ASD / 184 HC). | quote: \"Skipping subjects lacking ﬁlename, we downloaded 106, 175, 72, 71 subjects from UM1, NYU, USM, UCLA1 separately. HO parcellated each brain into 111 ROIs. Since some sub- jects did not contain complete ROIs, we removed the incom- plete data, resulting in 88, 167, 52, 63 subjects for UM1, NYU, USM, UCLA1 separately.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-020" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1171 ;
            slr:answer_text """predictive | ABIDE Preprocessed Connectomes Project release (consistent with ABIDE I's ~1112-subject pool); 1102 subjects downloaded, excluded those with missing imaging data, final N = 506 ASD / 548 TC across 17 sites | quote: "We successfully downloaded a dataset 
of 1102 subjects from the Preprocessed Connectomes Project, 
and then excluded subjects whose imaging data shows some miss-
ing. Finally, data of 506 ASD individuals and 548 controls was 
included in our study.\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-052" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1211 ;
            slr:answer_text """ABIDE-I, N=1112 initially; excluded for missing files, Stanford site (spiral acquisition), Leuven-1 site (unknown TR), PCP rater quality fail, and QC-FC association/distance-dependence checks; final n=395 ASD/425 TD (820 total). | quote: "After removing subjects based on these exclusion criteria, we were left with 395 subjects in the ASD group and 
425 subjects in the TD group\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-093" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1215 ;
            slr:answer_text "predictive | ABIDE I, 529 ASD and 573 TC (1102 total) from 17 sites, processed through four pipelines in parallel. | quote: \"We incorporated data from 529 ASD individuals and 573 typical controls (TC) for each pipeline, which is comprised of 17 different imaging sites.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-036" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1220 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE I, the same commonly-used 871-subject subset (403 ASD, 468 TC); no study-specific exclusion/QC rule is described beyond reusing this subset. | quote: \"we used the same 871 samples from the ABIDE 1 data set [23], [24], [25]. Of the 871 subjects, 403 patients were ASD and 468 were TC patients.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-069" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1258 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE I, 850 subjects (355 ASD with DSM-IV-TR diagnosis, 495 HC) from the same sites; no additional motion/QC exclusion rule beyond this stated in text. | quote: \"Resting-state fMRI data from 850 subjects in ABIDE I with an ASD DSM-IV-TR diagnosis (n = 355) and the corresponding HCs (n = 495) from the same sites were used in this study\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-098" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1167 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE-I, 17 sites, 1035 subjects (505 ASD, 530 HC) | quote: \"This dataset consists 1,035 rs-fMRI data with 505 ASD subject, and 530 healthy control subjects that are collected from 17 diﬀerent sites.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-028" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1199 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE I, UCLA site only: initially 49 ASD/33 TC, after removing participants with large head motion, final n=41 ASD/32 TC. | quote: \"Participants with large motions were removed from the dataset, resulting in 32 participants in the TC group and 41 in the ASD group.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-086" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1191 ;
            slr:answer_text """associational | ABIDE (consistent with ABIDE I, 7 sites including Caltech/CMU/NYU/Pitt/SDSU/Trinity/UCLA); 454 subjects with complete phenotypic data = 256 HC, 166 autism, 32 Asperger’s (198 ASD total); PDD-NOS and "Asperger’s or PDD-NOS" excluded to reduce class imbalance | quote: "Four hundred and ﬁfty-four subjects with complete phenotypic
data were selected from the Autism Brain Imaging Data
Exchange (ABIDE) database\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-075" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1251 ;
            slr:answer_text "descriptor — ABIDE II release: 1,044 datasets (ASD N=487, Controls N=557) across 17 collections/16 sites; no QC-based exclusion applied, all data released regardless of quality | quote: \"users regardless of data quality27. The rationale of this decision includes the lack of consensus on optimal quality criteria in regards to speciﬁc measures or their combinations and cutoffs.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-001" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1238 ;
            slr:answer_text """Two ABIDE I-derived multimodal cohorts: ABIDE A (871 subjects, 403 ASD/468 TC, following Parisot 2017) and ABIDE B (949 subjects, 419 ASD/530 TC, following Wang 2020); both inherit the selection/QC rules of those prior published protocols rather than defining a new one. | quote: "The dataset includes 871 subjects
(468 TC and 403 ASD subjects). We follow (Parisot, 2017) [19] for
the dataset settings and preprocessing.\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-066" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1212 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE I+II, all publicly available sites; N=1,017 ASD and 1,127 TD, age-stratified into 8 bins; no additional QC exclusion beyond the full public release. | quote: \"This study includes all sites publicly available through ABIDE I and ABIDE II. They were comprised of 1,127 TD and 1,017 ASD.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-088" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1168 ;
            slr:answer_text "associational | ABIDE I, 507 male subjects (209 ASD, 298 controls) from 14 sites, with FIQ and mean-FD each within 2 SD of the ABIDE-wide mean. | quote: \"Speciﬁcally, the 507 subjects included 209 subjects with ASD and 298 well-matched health controls across 14 sites from the Autism Brain Imaging Data Exchange (ABIDE).\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-044" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1206 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE I, single-site subsets: NYU (184 subjects: 79 ASD, 105 NC, primary) and UM (145 subjects: 68 ASD, 77 NC, secondary); sites chosen specifically to avoid inter-site heterogeneity, no further motion/QC rule stated. | quote: \"In this work, we use rs-fMRI data from the New York University (NYU) site with the largest sample size collected in this database. Speciﬁcally, the NYU site includes 184 subjects, 79 of whom were from ASD and 105 NC cases.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-059" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1185 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE I+II across 37 sites (30 sites in the site-correction procedure), initial 916 ASD/1067 CTL (1983 total), QC'd to 710 ASD (79% male) / 606 CTL (87% male), ages 5-64 | quote: \"After the removal of subjects with image artifacts, high head movement, or poor MNI152 coregistration, we analyzed the data from the remaining 710 ASD (79% male), and 606 CTL (87% male) subjects, whose age ranges from 5 to 64 years.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-015" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1190 ;
            slr:answer_text "associational | ABIDE I, 55 ASD and 55 age-matched controls accessed via NITRC/ABIDE; acquisition appears to be a single scanner/site (3T GE Signa, 32-channel coil), site not explicitly named. | quote: \"Anatomical and functional data from fifty-five subjects with ASD (12.7 ± 2.4 y/o) and 55 age- matched (14.1 ± 3.1 y/o) healthy controls were accessed through the NITRC database and the ABIDE project.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ1> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
            slr:source_id "S-045" ] ;
    slr:question_id "RQ1" ;
    slr:question_text "Which ABIDE release(s) and subset (N by diagnosis, sites, QC/exclusion rule) were analysed?" ;
    slr:theme "Cohort" .

<urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> a slr:ResearchQuestion ;
    dcterms:title "Pipeline and parcellation" ;
    slr:has_answer [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1202 ;
            slr:answer_text """Lab-made FSL pipeline (FSL-BET, FSL-BBreg, FSL-FNIRT, CompCor, dual regression), noted as similar to C-PAC; no ROI atlas, instead the Smith et al. 2009 RSN10 ICA template. | quote: "We subsequently applied 
dual-regression analysis18 by using the FSL general linear model (GLM) and the 10-brain resting-state networks 
(RSN10)\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-091" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1197 ;
            slr:answer_text "ABIDE Preprocessed Connectomes Project CPAC pipeline; four atlases compared (AAL, Harvard-Oxford, Craddock-200, Power). | quote: \"using the Configurable Pipeline for the Analysis of Connectomes (CPAC) (31), that includes slice- timing, motion correction, intensity normalization, nuisance signal removal\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-062" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1203 ;
            slr:answer_text "CPAC (Configurable Pipeline for Analysis of Connectomes) via the Preprocessed Connectomes Project, band-pass filter 0.01-0.1Hz, no global signal regression; Harvard-Oxford atlas (111 ROIs) primary, Craddock CC200 (200 ROIs) as a replication atlas. | quote: \"we downloaded Re- gions of Interests (ROIs) fMRI series of the top four largest sites (UM1, NYU, USM, UCLA1) from the preprocessed ABIDE dataset with Conﬁgurable Pipeline for the Analysis of Connec- tomes (CPAC), band-pass ﬁltering (0.01 - 0.1 Hz), no global signal regression, parcellated by Harvard-Oxford (HO) atlas.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-020" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1238 ;
            slr:answer_text """C-PAC pipeline; ABIDE A uses CC200-based fMRI connection networks (Parisot 2017 setup), ABIDE B uses three atlases — CC200, AAL, Dosenbach160. | quote: "The dataset integrates three brain atlases (CC200,
AAL - Automated Anatomical Labeling, and DOS - Dosenbach160)\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-066" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1235 ;
            slr:answer_text """DPARSF preprocessing (discard first 5 volumes, slice-timing, motion realignment, MNI normalization, 8mm FWHM smoothing); AAL atlas (116 ROIs, 22 DMN ROIs used). | quote: "The DPARSF is a MATLAB toolbox for fMRI data pre-
processing and analysing [17].\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-097" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1212 ;
            slr:answer_text "No connectivity pipeline/atlas used; head-motion (linear/angular speed) parameters derived directly from rs-fMRI realignment, analyzed via custom Gamma-distribution/stochastic signature methods." ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-088" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1259 ;
            slr:answer_text "DPARSF pipeline (SPM8-based, 24-parameter motion/WM/CSF regression, bandpass filtering); three atlases used jointly — AAL (116 ROIs), CC200 (200 ROIs), Dosenbach160. | quote: \"METAFormer employs a multi-atlas approach, where flattened connectivity matrices from the AAL, CC200, and DOS160 atlases serve as input to the transformer encoder.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-074" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1252 ;
            slr:answer_text "No connectivity pipeline or atlas; raw 3D NIfTI volumes converted to 2D axial-plane image slices with MRIcron for direct CNN input. | quote: \"MRIcron software was used to convert the  3D data format into 2D data images.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-056" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1208 ;
            slr:answer_text "C-PAC pipeline, volumes downsampled to 4mm MNI; no ROI atlas or connectivity feature extraction — the model operates on raw 4D volumes. | quote: \"We preprocessed the data with the Conﬁgurable Pipeline for the Analysis of Connectomes (C-PAC) and the fMRI volumes are downsampled to 4 mm in MNI.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-058" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1225 ;
            slr:answer_text "C-PAC pipeline, regional homogeneity (ReHo) derivative from the Preprocessed Connectomes Project; no ROI atlas (voxel-wise, grey-matter masked). | quote: \"We speciﬁcally focused on the regional homogeneity (ReHo) fMRI derivative (Zang et al. 2004) from the Conﬁgurable Pipeline for the Analysis of Connectomes (CPAC) pipeline\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-081" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1190 ;
            slr:answer_text "Custom AFNI-based pipeline (3dWarpDrive motion correction, N27 atlas spatial warping); TT_Daemon atlas (240 ROIs) for ROI-level analysis. | quote: \"The 240 regions of interest (ROIs) defined for this study were extracted from the TT_Daemon human brain atlas [43] provided with the AFNI package [44].\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-045" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1206 ;
            slr:answer_text "DPARSF pipeline (head motion correction, nuisance regression, MNI standardization, band-pass filter); two parcellations used for multi-scale representation — AAL (116 ROIs) and CC200 (200 ROIs). | quote: \"by partitioning the brain into multiple ROIs using two atlases, i.e., Automated Anatomical Labeling (AAL) (Tzourio-Mazoyer et al., 2002) atlas with 116 ROIs and Craddock200 (CC200) (Craddock et al., 2012) atlas with 200 ROIs.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-059" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1204 ;
            slr:answer_text "Freesurfer v6.0 recon-all (Desikan-Killiany-Tourville atlas) for structural; C-PAC for functional with Harvard-Oxford atlas (103 regions after exclusion) | quote: \"The rs-fMRI scans selected from ABIDE I and ABIDE II cohorts were processed with the Configurable Pipe- line for the Analysis of Connectomes (C-PAC) [20]\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-016" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1236 ;
            slr:answer_text "CPAC (Configurable Pipeline for Analysis of Connectomes) via the Preprocessed Connectomes Project, v1.0.2a for ABIDE-II, with global signal regression and band-pass filtering; seven atlases: HO, EZ, TT, CC200, CC400, AAL, DOS160. | quote: \"The Preprocessed Connectomes Project (PCP) released preprocessed versions of ABIDE using several pipelines [4]. We used the data processed through Conﬁgurable Pipeline for Analysis of Connectomes (CPAC). This pipeline includes slice timing correction, motion correction, global mean intensity normalization and standardization of functional data to MNI space (3x3x3 mm resolution) before the extraction of ROI time series.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-006" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1240 ;
            slr:answer_text "Athena pipeline; no cortical parcellation atlas named — analysis uses 65 cortical ROIs regressed against cerebellar principal components, not a specific named cortical atlas in the extracted text | quote: \"We preprocessed the imaging data using the Athena pipeline (www.nitrc.org/plugins/mwiki/index.php/neurobureau:Athena Pipeline). The pipeline focused on providing systematic processing of fMRI data, including the following main steps: exclusion of the ﬁrst four scans; slice timing correction;\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-012" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1193 ;
            slr:answer_text "C-PAC pipeline (slice-time/motion correction, CompCor, band-pass 0.01-0.1Hz, no GSR); surface-based Conte69 template, no standard ROI atlas. | quote: \"based on  the configurable pipeline for the analysis of connectomes  (C-PAC) (https://fcp-indi.github.io/) [83]\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-080" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1201 ;
            slr:answer_text "Connectome Computation System (CCS) pipeline; Automated Anatomical Labeling (AAL) atlas (90 ROIs, 4,005 FC links); Pearson correlation connectivity with site/age/gender/handedness regressed out via OLS. | quote: \"The rs- fMRI data were processed using Connectome Computation System (Xu et al., 2015) pipeline, which includes slice timing correction, motion realignment, and intensity normalization. Nuisance variable regression (Fox et al., 2005; Lund et al., 2005) was implemented through band-pass ﬁltering and global signal regression strategies to clean confounding variations introduced by heartbeats and respirations, head motion, and low frequency scanner drifts. Furthermore, boundary-based rigid body and FMRIB’s linear & nonlinear image registration tools (Andersson et al., 2008; Ratziu et al., 2008) were used to register functional to anatomical images. Then, both functional and anatomical images were normalized to a standard template space, the Automated Anatomical Labeling atlas (Tzourio-Mazoyer et al., 2002).\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-025" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1174 ;
            slr:answer_text "Custom SPM12/DARTEL preprocessing pipeline (realignment, normalization, smoothing, band-pass filter, scrubbing); 200-ROI Craddock atlas for connectivity matrices | quote: \"Data presented in this study underwent standard fMRI pre- processing (i.e., realignment, normalization, and smoothing) implemented in SPM12b. Data were preprocessed according to standard SPM protocols including realignment, normalization to a study specific template using DARTEL, smoothing, band- pass filtering (0.01–0.05 Hz), and scrubbing to account for head movements (63).\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-029" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1196 ;
            slr:answer_text """C-PAC pipeline; AAL90 atlas (90 ROIs). | quote: "The selected mean time-series
correspond to the Automated Anatomical Labeling atlas on 90 regions of interest
(AAL90)\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-055" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1226 ;
            slr:answer_text "CPAC pipeline (one of four Preprocessed Connectomes Project pipelines); three atlases: AAL (116 ROIs), Craddock 200 (CC), Eickhoff-Zilles (EZ) | quote: \"We, therefore, leverage the CPAC pipeline, hereinafter referred to as the ABIDE I CPAC data.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-014" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1230 ;
            slr:answer_text "C-PAC (Preprocessed Connectomes Project); atlases compared: Harvard-Oxford, Yeo, ICA, MSDL, K-Means, Ward. | quote: \"We speciﬁcally used the data processed with the Conﬁgurable Pipeline for the Analysis of Connectomes [34] (C-PAC).\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-002" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1241 ;
            slr:answer_text "C-PAC pipeline; Harvard-Oxford (HO) atlas. | quote: \"the mean time series for a set of regions extracted from the Harvard Oxford (HO) atlas (Desikan et al., 2006) were computed\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-019" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1246 ;
            slr:answer_text """DPARSF pipeline (slice timing, head-movement correction, normalization, smoothing, band-pass filter, nuisance regression); AAL atlas (116 ROIs). | quote: "we used the data Processing As-
sistant for Resting-State fMRI (DPARSF) t\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-090" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1177 ;
            slr:answer_text "No named standard ABIDE pipeline (e.g. CPAC/DPARSF) — iFC was computed using the same in-house SPM-based seed-based procedure as the original (non-ABIDE) sample; analysis is seed-based (right pSTS seed), not atlas/parcellation-based. | quote: \"For the ABIDE-replication dataset (278 ASD/306 TD participants) (Supplementary Table S1), we computed iFC and mean FD scores using the same procedures as described above (Supplementary Figure S3B). Within each site, groups displayed comparable mean FD scores (except for one site). Across sites, micro-movements were greater within the ASD than in the TD group [F(1,566) ¼ 4.23, P ¼ 0.041] (Supplementary Table S1 and Figure S3B). As for the ori- ginal sample, we corrected for micro-movements by including mean FD scores as a nuisance covariate in the primary group analysis\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-026" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1243 ;
            slr:answer_text """C-PAC pipeline, Harvard-Oxford atlas | quote: "For preprocessing of
the ABIDE dataset, we use the Configurable Pipeline for the
Analysis of Connectomes (C-PAC) [41]\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-077" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1185 ;
            slr:answer_text "C-PAC v1.8.0 pipeline; 11-region Brodmann-area atlas parcellation of fALFF and ReHo maps | quote: \"The package CPAC v1.8.0 was used for fMRI pre-processing including head motion correction, scrubbing, and nuisance regression.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-015" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1179 ;
            slr:answer_text "CPAC pipeline; no ROI atlas — raw downsampled 4D spatio-temporal fMRI volumes (28x28x28x32) used directly | quote: \"The preprocessing method used in this paper is the conﬁgurable pipeline for the analysis of connectomes (CPAC)\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-070" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1229 ;
            slr:answer_text "CPAC (Configurable Pipeline for the Analysis of Connectomes) via the Preprocessed Connectomes Project; AAL atlas (116 ROIs); multiple connectivity measures (Spearman, percentage-bend and partial correlation, SICE, mutual information). | quote: \"we used the preprocessed version of ABIDE I (Di Martino et al., 2014) data publicly available via the Preprocessed Connectome Project (Cameron et al., 2013b). The preprocessing pipeline we used for this study is the Conﬁgurable Pipeline for the Analysis of Connectomes (CPAC) (Cameron et al., 2013a). Regions of interests (ROIs) were deﬁned as the 116 regions in the automatic anatomical labeling (AAL) atlas (Tzourio-Mazoyer et al., 2002).\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
            slr:source_id "S-033" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1171 ;
            slr:answer_text """C-PAC pipeline (Preprocessed Connectomes Project), CC200 atlas | quote: "The rs-fMRI data utilized in this study was preprocessed with 
the Configurable Pipeline for the Analysis of Conenectomes (C-
PAC).\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ2> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ2" ;
