        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1201 ;
            slr:answer_text "5-fold stratified CV per target site; a multiple-regression site/age/gender/handedness correction applied to FC features; offline SSAE pretraining confined to the 16 non-target ABIDE sites to avoid leaking target-site data into pretraining. | quote: \"the independent healthy FC data from the remaining 16 sites from the ABIDE repository were accumulated as pre- collected data to train an SSAE prototype during oﬄine learning. Then, we randomly split the data from the target site into training and testing set. The data from the training set were applied on an SSAE prototype in the prior knowledge aided training step. The hold-out testing data were then used to evaluate the trained DTL-NN model.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-025" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1240 ;
            slr:answer_text "Linear regression (GLM) per cortical ROI vs. cerebellar PCs, with site as covariate; Benjamini-Hochberg FDR correction across 65 tests (significance threshold 5%); validated via an independent-sample (ABIDE II) replication rather than leave-site-out cross-validation | quote: \"Thus, to minimize the site eﬀect in our analysis, we included it as a covariate in group-level statistics as described in the section 2.3.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-012" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1250 ;
            slr:answer_text "Pooled 10-fold cross-validation mixing all 17 sites in fixed proportion (not leave-site-out); supplementary per-site 5-fold cross-validation also reported; no statistical correction stated. | quote: \"a 10-fold cross-validation schema that mixes data from all 17 sites while keeping\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-076" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1211 ;
            slr:answer_text """Two-tailed two-sample t-tests with FDR correction (alpha=0.05) for brain-wide and node-level curvature comparisons across 49 graph densities (2-50%); single cohort analysis (not cross-validated/predictive, no leave-site-out). | quote: "we employed a two-tailed two-sample t test 
followed by FDR correction\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-093" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1177 ;
            slr:answer_text "Two-sample group comparison of right pSTS seed-based iFC with mean framewise displacement included as a nuisance covariate; small-volume and whole-brain FWE-corrected statistics; a secondary motion-scrubbed analysis was run as a sensitivity check. | quote: \"For the ABIDE-replication dataset (278 ASD/306 TD participants) (Supplementary Table S1), we computed iFC and mean FD scores using the same procedures as described above (Supplementary Figure S3B). Within each site, groups displayed comparable mean FD scores (except for one site). Across sites, micro-movements were greater within the ASD than in the TD group [F(1,566) ¼ 4.23, P ¼ 0.041] (Supplementary Table S1 and Figure S3B). As for the ori- ginal sample, we corrected for micro-movements by including mean FD scores as a nuisance covariate in the primary group analysis\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-026" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1196 ;
            slr:answer_text """Leave-One-Out Cross-Validation with inner cross-validation for hyperparameter tuning on each training split; no leave-site-out evaluation reported despite 17 contributing sites. | quote: "Tuning is performed through an inner
cross-validation launched on each training split to select the best corresponding parameter value.\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-055" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1207 ;
            slr:answer_text "Spectral dynamic causal modelling (spDCM) per subject, second-level group analysis via Parametric Empirical Bayes (PEB); single site (KKI), no cross-site or leave-site-out evaluation (single site study). | quote: \"Parametric empirical Bayesian (PEB) was used to perform second-level group analysis\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-082" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1242 ;
            slr:answer_text "A single random 70/30 train/test split (58/26 subjects); the number of base SVMs and the feature-set dimensionality were both tuned by maximising accuracy on the same 26-subject test set, which was then reported as the final accuracy; no cross-validation or independent validation set was used. | quote: \"Firstly, the 84 samples are divided into 58 training samples and 26 test samples based on the ratio of 7:3. Then 50 samples are randomly selected from the 58 training samples and 62 features are randomly selected from 4,225 features, which form a single SVM using Radial Basis Function (RBF) as kernel provided by the SVM toolbox (http://see.xidian.edu.cn/faculty/chzheng/ bishe/indexﬁles/indexl.htm) (Gunn, 1998). The width argument of RBF equals to 3, and penalty coeﬃcient equals to Inf. The process is repeated for 500 times and these 500 SVMs constitute into a random SVM cluster.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-027" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1262 ;
            slr:answer_text """Wilcoxon rank-sum tests for group comparisons (FC PCA scores, motion equivalence); multilinear/elastic-net regression of FC-PCA scores on RSN entropy with 10-fold cross-validation; single ABIDE cohort pooled across sites, no leave-site-out evaluation. | quote: "The minimum MSE computed from a 10-fold cross validation
was 11.4 ± 7.2% of c1 variance, and was observed for α = 0.15.\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-094" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1259 ;
            slr:answer_text """10-fold stratified cross-validation with 30% of each training fold held out as a separate validation set for hyperparameter tuning/early stopping, distinct from the held-out test fold; no site covariate, harmonisation, or leave-site-out evaluation reported for the pooled 17-site cohort. | quote: "we employed 10-fold stratified cross-validation. For each fold, the model is trained
on the remaining nine training folds and evaluated on the held-out test fold.
Further, we set aside 30% of each training fold as validation sets\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-074" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1239 ;
            slr:answer_text "70/15/15 train/validation/test split with early stopping, plus 10-fold cross-validation for mean test accuracy; no site covariate or leave-site-out evaluation | quote: \"10-fold cross validation was used and the mean test accuracy was calculated.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-063" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1167 ;
            slr:answer_text "10-fold cross-validation on the whole dataset; separate 5-fold cross-validation per site to assess generalisability; no explicit leave-one-site-out evaluation or site harmonisation in the main model | quote: \"we chose k as 10 to perform 10-fold cross validation using the whole dataset.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-028" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1202 ;
            slr:answer_text """Two-sample t-tests with FWE correction (FSL-randomise, 5000 permutations) for ABIDE group differences; Pearson correlation with FDR-adjusted p-values and ROC/AUC analysis in the KMUH validation cohort; no site covariate or leave-site-out scheme for the pooled ABIDE derivation step. | quote: "FC val-
ues significantly different [family-wise error (FWE)-corrected p < 0.05] between the ASD and TD groups\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-091" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1258 ;
            slr:answer_text """Group difference evaluated via Hedge's g effect size at literature-selected ROI pairs (MPFC-PCC/precuneus; frontal pole-temporal lobe), comparing original data, GLM, ComBat, and the proposed site-wise de-meaning (SWD); age and sex regressed out beforehand; no whole-brain multiple-comparison-corrected statistical test reported for this analysis. | quote: "The resting state fMRI data was then parcellated into
200 regions of interest (ROIs)\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-098" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1199 ;
            slr:answer_text "Pairwise Pearson correlations (4005 pairs) tested with local false-discovery-rate (fdr q=0.1) and Network Based Statistics (permutation p=0.05) multiple-comparison correction; single site, no cross-validation or leave-site-out (not a predictive study). | quote: \"the multiple testing correction methods including local fdr and Network Based Statistics (NBS) performed for both empirical Bayes normalized correlations and original correlations\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-086" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1169 ;
            slr:answer_text "Propensity-score stratified train/holdout partitioning (contiguous/diverse/random schemes) with 10-fold CV within training strata; out-of-distribution evaluation in held-out strata; no explicit leave-site-out, but site is one of the matched/propensity covariates; deconfounding (linear regression, ComBat) tested but computed on all participants rather than training folds only | quote: \"Similar to the computation of the pro- pensity scores, we performed deconfounding prior to our analyses, based on all the available participants instead of using only the training\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-011" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1226 ;
            slr:answer_text "10-fold cross-validation on each of three dataset variants (whole ABIDE I, a selector-defined 'proposed subset', and the NYU site subset); F-score feature selection described as computed on all features in the dataset rather than confined to training folds; no leave-site-out evaluation" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-014" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1260 ;
            slr:answer_text "No train/test split ratio or cross-validation scheme is reported; evaluation is reported separately per site/resource subset rather than leave-site-out | quote: \"ABIDE-II data download and labelling was a   challenging task. Each image was manually labelled and   assigned a group. Each group was tested separately to compare and analyze results of each set.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-004" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1229 ;
            slr:answer_text "10-fold cross-validation within each of five age groups; sequential (wrapper) feature selection reduced 817 features to 10; models compared via 10x10 Welch's t-tests with FDR correction; no explicit site covariate or harmonisation across the pooled multi-site sample. | quote: \"We minimized the risk of overﬁtting by using three limiting approaches. First, the simplest kernel (linear) was used for the SVM. Second, only 10 features were used to learn to classify between 104 subjects. Finally, using 10-fold cross validation ensured the model is only evaluated on data points that it has not experienced before.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-033" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1168 ;
            slr:answer_text "Two-tailed two-sample t-tests with Bonferroni correction across 19 HMM states, reported both with and without regressing out site and FIQ; site x group interaction effects explicitly checked via a data-driven subject-matching algorithm. | quote: \"two-tailed two-sample, Bonferroni correction\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-044" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1165 ;
            slr:answer_text "Voxel-wise GLM with diagnosis/sex/interaction as regressors and age+mFD as covariates; voxel-level Z>3.1, cluster-level P<0.01 (Bonferroni-equivalent 0.05/5 metrics); robustness checked across alternate pipelines; no leave-site-out evaluation, but site effects removed via ComBat and findings checked for site consistency | quote: \"Discovery analyses in ABIDE revealed significant main effects of diagnosis and sex across the intrinsic func‑ tional connectivity of the posterior cingulate cortex, regional homogeneity and voxel-mirrored homotopic connectiv‑ ity (VMHC) in several cortical regions, largely converging in the default network midline.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-008" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1166 ;
            slr:answer_text "Novel statistical graph network-detection/testing algorithm applied to the full sample to identify abnormal subnetworks, then SVM (RBF/linear) with leave-one-out cross-validation used to validate classification accuracy; single site, so no site covariate/leave-site-out needed | quote: \"The leave-one-out cross-validation results show that the accuracy rates are 89 and 84% correspondingly.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-078" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1257 ;
            slr:answer_text "5-fold CV within the 70% training set for hyperparameter selection, with final evaluation on a untouched 30% hold-out set; significance assessed via binomial tests (vs. chance and vs. prior state-of-the-art) and McNemar tests; an explicit site-confound check compared a site-only baseline classifier and re-evaluated on site-balanced test sets. | quote: \"We found that models trained using only site information achieved an accuracy of 66.0% on the ADHD data and 55.0% on the ABIDE data, while our models trained on MRI data achieved much higher accuracies: 67.4% and 64.3%, respectively.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-023" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1204 ;
            slr:answer_text "Nested 10-fold cross-validation (training in inner loop, AUC/accuracy evaluated in outer loop); SHAP feature importance computed within the inner loop; site harmonization via NeuroHarmonize fit on the whole cohort before CV | quote: \"The model was trained to distinguish subjects with ASD from TD according to a nested 10-fold cross-validation scheme.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-016" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1227 ;
            slr:answer_text "Intra-site 5-fold cross-validation (pooled and site-balanced) and inter-site leave-one-site-out cross-validation; accuracy, sensitivity and specificity reported; no statistical correction stated. | quote: \"For inter-site, we employed a leave- one-out-site approach that involved training the classiﬁer on all the sites except the one left out for testing.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-072" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1171 ;
            slr:answer_text """10-fold cross-validation with nested CV for hyperparameters; feature selection (top 1935 features) described prior to the CV split; a separate intra-site stratified shuffle-split CV was run to probe site effects (not leave-site-out) | quote: "we utilized 10-
fold cross-validation to measure the accuracy of predicted label. 
Any hyper-parameter operated in the method was internally set 
in the nested cross-validation.\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-052" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1195 ;
            slr:answer_text "Voxel-wise 2-tailed t-test with age and sex as covariates; FDR-corrected P<0.05 with minimum cluster size of 20 voxels; Benjamini-Hochberg correction for clinical-correlation analyses; no site covariate or leave-site-out evaluation reported | quote: \"2-tailed t-test design with two covariates of age and sex was used to compute the statistical signiﬁcance of the FCD diﬀerences between the two groups. Statistical signiﬁcance was based on the false discovery rate corrected P < 0.05 together with requiring 20 voxels for the minimum continuous voxel size within a cluster (corrected P < 0.05).\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-041" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1230 ;
            slr:answer_text "Leave-one-site-out cross-validation for inter-site evaluation, intra-site CV also reported, nested CV for hyperparameters, ROI estimation confined to training folds. | quote: \"Note that the ROI were all deﬁned on the training set to avoid possible overﬁtting.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-002" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1219 ;
            slr:answer_text """Five-fold cross-validation is stated generically for the model; no ABIDE-specific leakage-control, site-handling or leave-site-out statement is given. | quote: "Five-fold 
cross-validation is used to evaluate the performance of the 
model.\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-049" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1215 ;
            slr:answer_text "Single random 85%/15% train/test split; separate per-site (unit-site) classification performed to assess site variability; no cross-validation or leave-site-out scheme reported for the main model. | quote: \"we ﬁrst divided the whole dataset into two parts: training (85%), and testing (15%).\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-036" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1185 ;
            slr:answer_text "Fisher r-to-z test of ASD vs CTL correlation differences, combined by Fisher's method, Benjamini-Hochberg FDR correction; age/site/sex regressed out by linear model, site-mean correction applied | quote: \"To reduce the impact of confounders, we regressed out age, site, and sex using a linear model.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-015" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1243 ;
            slr:answer_text "Stratified 10-fold cross-validation with grid-search hyperparameter tuning on the training set; feature reduction (recursive feature elimination) described before the CV section; site used as a population-graph edge-weight feature rather than a covariate or leave-site-out split | quote: \"We use a stratified 10-fold cross-validation strategy.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-077" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1233 ;
            slr:answer_text "Two-sample t-tests on ROI-to-ROI connectivity; mean FD, FSIQ and imaging site included as nuisance covariates; Bonferroni correction (p=0.004) in the ABIDE II replication test; original dataset used voxel-height p<0.001 with FDR-corrected cluster threshold p<0.05. | quote: \"mean FD scores were included as a nuisance covariate in t-tests. In addition, FSIQ and imaging sites were included as nuisance covariates. Bonferroni correction was performed for multiple comparisons (p = 0.004).\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-043" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1183 ;
            slr:answer_text """10-fold cross-validation; single-site design (not multi-site, so no leave-site-out); no explicit leakage-control statement for the group-ICA/dual-regression feature derivation step | quote: "A total of 10-fold cross validation strategy was used for evaluating classiﬁcation
performance.\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-060" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1253 ;
            slr:answer_text "CPM edge selection (motion/site-masked), with leave-one-out cross-validation (N-1 per iteration) and split-half cross-validation; significance assessed by permutation testing (5000 shuffles) rather than parametric r-to-p conversion. | quote: \"a leave-one-out cross-validation to evaluate the potential of models to predict  14  an unseen participant’s score\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-092" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1191 ;
            slr:answer_text "Cluster similarity percentage across GA/SFS/SFR feature selection and DPC/OPTICS/hierarchical clustering combinations; explicitly no cross-validation during clustering; no site-specific/leave-site-out evaluation possible for ASD | quote: \"we did not perform cross-validation during clustering.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ4> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ4" ;
            slr:source_id "S-075" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1190 ;
            slr:answer_text "Voxel-wise Z-scoring (|Z|>2.0 threshold) and region-wise comparisons with reported p-values; Pearson correlation (PPMC) between ROI Z-scores and ADI-R/ADOS scores; no explicit multiple-comparisons correction described. | quote: \"We found that the main regions, where signal complexity significantly decreased among ASD patients, were the amygdala (p = 0.001), the vermis (p = 0.02), the basal ganglia (p = 0.01) and the hippocampus (p = 0.02).\"" ;
