        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1222 ;
            slr:answer_text "5-fold CV: ~60-66% balanced accuracy across models, best for the MM-ensemble (64%/66% F1) and the ReHo single measure; leave-site-out CV: MM-ensemble dropped to 56% balanced accuracy/59% F1, with good performance only at the NYU site, showing that pooled cross-validation substantially overestimates cross-site generalisation. | quote: \"When assessed by ﬁve-fold CV procedure, all tested models performed at around 60% accuracy for the classiﬁcation task (Figure 2 and Table 2), with little variation between models' performances. On the contrary, the leave-site-out CV procedure shows high variability in terms of model performances with relatively good performance for the NYU site and poor performance for the other sites\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-030" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1262 ;
            slr:answer_text """FC imbalance across 11 RSNs in ASD (p=0.002) corresponded to a weaker FC-entropy relationship (p=0.02); entropy-model fit distinguished ASD from controls (p=0.01) and correlated with ASD symptom severity (p=0.003). | quote: "Further, we observed that an estimated RSN entropy model
signiﬁcantly distinguished ASD from controls (p = 0.01) and was associated with level of
ASD symptom severity (p = 0.003).\"""" ;
