            slr:answer_text """HCAN achieved ACC 82.9%, SEN 76.7%, SPE 86.6%, AUC 84.6% on pooled 10-fold CV; per-site 5-fold CV mean ACC/SEN/SPE/AUC = 75.6%/72.6%/77.3%/83.0%. | quote: "The proposed HCAN method achieves an average ACC of 82.9%, 
SEN of 76.7%, SPE of 86.6% and AUC of 84.6%.\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-076" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1180 ;
            slr:answer_text "k-nn accuracy 62.9% (all sites) with the GCN distance metric vs. 51.0% with PCA/Euclidean distance, an 11.9-point improvement; larger gains for individual sites (up to 90.0% vs 50.0% for site 18). | quote: \"PCA/Euclidean 51.0% 59.3% 25.0% 30.0% 64.3% 50.0% GCN 62.9% 81.5% 62.5% 70.0% 50.0% 90.0%\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-024" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1203 ;
            slr:answer_text "Federated learning (Fed) achieved higher accuracy than the best cross-site model at every site (NYU 0.647, UM 0.728, USM 0.849, UCLA 0.712 with the HO atlas) and was significantly better than single-site training (p<0.001), approaching pooled (Mix) performance without sharing raw data; domain adaptation (Fed-MoE/Fed-Align) gave further improvement at most sites. | quote: \"Single 0.601(0.064) 0.648(0.065) 0.695(0.108) 0.571(0.100) Ensemble 0.611(0.012) 0.638(0.054) 0.654(0.088) 0.634(0.064) Fed 0.647(0.049) 0.728(0.073) 0.849(0.124) 0.712(0.075) Fed-MoE 0.671(0.082) 0.728(0.083) 0.809(0.098) 0.744(0.130) Fed-Align 0.676(0.071) 0.751(0.053) 0.829(0.091) 0.712(0.089) Mix 0.671(0.035) 0.740(0.063) 0.829(0.137) 0.710(0.128) Table 3: Results of using diﬀerent training strategies\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-020" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1188 ;
            slr:answer_text "Average accuracy 0.735 (sensitivity 0.765, specificity 0.752) across three atlas-based datasets; best per-atlas accuracy 83.82% (CC atlas); no AUC or CI reported. | quote: \"our developed MHOA based on the SSDAE model has accuracy 66.35%, 70.19%, and 83.82% for EZ, AAL, and CC, respectively.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-064" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1185 ;
            slr:answer_text "415 differentially correlated genes identified (Diff Cor P<0.01, CTL FDR<0.05), effect size >1.8 for ~3% of expressed genes, with regional emphasis on primary visual and inferior temporal cortex | quote: \"415 differentially corre- lated genes (DC genes; Diff Cor P < 0.01, CTL FDR < 0.05\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-015" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1257 ;
            slr:answer_text "Combined model (LEFMSF) achieved 0.643 hold-out accuracy on ABIDE, the best known result using imaging data alone, exceeding prior published results by 0.042; a site-only classifier achieved only 55.0% accuracy on ABIDE (near chance) and accuracy on a site-balanced test set (63.46%) was similar to the original, indicating the result is not a site-composition artifact. | quote: \"achieving an accuracy of 0.673 on the ADHD-200 holdout data and 0.643 on the ABIDE holdout data. Both of these results, obtained with the same LEFMSF framework, are the best known, over all hold-out accuracies on these datasets when only using imaging data—exceeding previously-published results by 0.012 for ADHD and 0.042 for Autism.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-023" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1207 ;
            slr:answer_text "ASD children showed decreased effective connectivity among VN, DMN, cerebellum, SMN and FPN vs TC; DMN(ANG_R)-to-SMN(PreCG_L) connectivity correlated negatively with ADOS stereotyped-behavior scores. | quote: \"children with ASD showed decreased effective connectivity among some large- scale brain networks. These brain networks included VN, DMN, cerebellum, SMN, and FPN.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-082" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1246 ;
            slr:answer_text """ASD-HNet achieved accuracy 73.57%, sensitivity 72.63%, specificity 74.90%, F1 71.04%, the best among all compared methods (paired t-test p<0.05 for each comparison). | quote: "ASD-HNet
73.57
72.63
74.90
71.04
-\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
