        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1219 ;
            slr:answer_text """Functional connectivity in SMN, and between DMN-DAN and DMN-FPN, identified as most important for ASD prediction; no numeric accuracy/AUC value specific to the ASD/ABIDE classification is given in the extracted text. | quote: "the
attention score in the SMN region is high, indicating that
connectivity plays a crucial role in ASD prediction in SMN.\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-049" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1168 ;
            slr:answer_text "ASD showed decreased fractional occupancy in HMM states 4, 8, 9, 10 and increased occupancy in states 2, 3, 14, 17 versus controls. | quote: \"compared to HCs, we found that fractional occupancies of HMM states 4, 8, 9, and 10 for ASD subjects were signiﬁcantly decreased\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-044" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1244 ;
            slr:answer_text "Subtype-unique subcortical fALFF alterations (direction given in q8) correlated with ADOS subdomains (social interaction common to all subtypes); prediction models generalized from ABIDE II to ABIDE I only for the matching subtype | quote: \"models can be generalized to predict ADOS and SRS scores for the corresponding subgroup from ABIDE I, but not for the other groups\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-009" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1208 ;
            slr:answer_text "3DCNN C-LSTM outperformed compared models on single sites (NYU accuracy 0.77/F1 0.78; UM accuracy 0.71/F1 0.70) but showed degraded performance on the multi-site ABIDE-I evaluation (accuracy 0.58/F1 0.53), attributed to scanner/acquisition heterogeneity. | quote: \"The results show that the proposed architecture 3DCNN C-LSTM outperforms other models on single site experiments by achieving mean test accuracies and F1 scores of 0.77 and 0.78 respectively for the NYU site and 0.71 and 0.7 on the UM site.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-058" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1169 ;
            slr:answer_text "In ABIDE, prediction performance declined as diversity increased: within-distribution AUC r=-0.630 (F1 r=-0.568), out-of-distribution AUC r=-0.671 (F1 r=-0.579); opposite relationship found in the HBN cohort | quote: \"we can observe a decline in performance in ABIDE as diversity increased in both within (AUC: r = −0.630, F1 score: r = −0.568) and out-of-distribution (AUC: r = −0.671, F1 score: r = −0.579) predictions.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-011" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1242 ;
            slr:answer_text "The random SVM cluster achieved 96.15% test accuracy with an optimal 272-feature set, substantially higher than a single SVM; discriminative regions included inferior frontal gyrus, hippocampus and precuneus. | quote: \"the accuracy of the random SVM cluster is as high as 96.15%. This is suﬃcient to show that the performance of the random SVM cluster is much better than a single SVM.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-027" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1258 ;
            slr:answer_text "SWD improved the ASD-vs-control effect size by 2.9-5.3% relative to the original (uncorrected) data, while GLM and ComBat decreased it by up to 11.4%, for the literature-anchored anterior-posterior DMN hypoconnectivity finding (MPFC-PCC/precuneus, MPFC-MTG). | quote: \"For the ABIDE dataset, SWD improved the effect size between autistic and control subjects by 2.9–5.3%, while GLM and ComBat decreased the effect size by up to 11.4%.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-098" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1172 ;
            slr:answer_text "ASD showed higher mean (Cohen's d=.18) and lower SD (d=-.19) of whole-brain modular variability; regionally higher variability in default-mode regions (d=.19-.33) and lower in visual cortex (d=-.24 to -.19), FDR p<.05; modular variability predicted SRS scores (r=.16, pperm=.002) | quote: \"the ASD group showed higher modular variability mainly in several default-mode regions, including the medial prefrontal cortex, posterior cingulate gyrus, and angular gyrus (Cohen’s d ranging from .19 to .33), and lower variability primarily in the visual cortex (Cohen’s d ranging from -.24 to -.19) (FDR corrected p < .05)\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-005" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1197 ;
            slr:answer_text "Hyper-connectivity in ASD between right angular gyrus-precuneus (DMN) and right frontal operculum-left IFG; best leave-one-site-out classification AUC 0.75±0.05 (HO atlas), best single fold AUC 0.83. | quote: \"The mean L-SVM classification performance, in terms of the area under the ROC curve (AUC), was 0.75 ± 0.05.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-062" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1259 ;
            slr:answer_text "Pretrained METAFormer achieved accuracy 83.7±3.0% and AUC 0.832±0.032, outperforming non-pretrained and single-atlas transformer variants as well as previously published ASD classifiers evaluated with 10-fold cross-validation on comparably sized ABIDE I samples. | quote: \"METAFormer PT 0.837 ±0.030 0.819±0.045 0.901 ±0.044 0.856 ±0.023 0.832 ±0.032\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-074" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1230 ;
            slr:answer_text "Best inter-site accuracy 66.8% (chance 53.7%) with MSDL + tangent embedding + l2-regularized classifier; abstract reports up to 67%. | quote: \"the highest accuracy obtained on the whole dataset is 66.8% (see Table 2) which ex- ceeds previously published ABIDE ﬁndings [53, 13, 54] and chance at 53.7%\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-002" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1240 ;
            slr:answer_text "Hypoconnectivity: reduced cortico-cerebellar connectivity in ASD vs TD in five ROIs in ABIDE I discovery (right fusiform, right postcentral, right/left middle temporal, right superior temporal gyri), 3 of 5 (right fusiform, right superior temporal, left middle temporal) replicated in ABIDE II (p=0.047, 0.002, 0.025 respectively, FDR-corrected) | quote: \"In this validation analysis, three out of ﬁve cortical ROIs, namely, the right fusiform gyrus [β = −0.028, t-value = −2.193, p = 0.047 —t-test (GLM)], the right superior temporal gyrus [β = −0.044, t-value = −3.495, p = 0.002 —t-test (GLM)], and the left middle temporal gyrus [β = −0.033, t-value = −2.583, p = 0.025—t-test (GLM)], conﬁrmed the reduced functional connectivity in the ASD group\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-012" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1228 ;
            slr:answer_text "EAG-RS achieved AUC 0.760±0.033, accuracy 73.71±2.83%, sensitivity 64.56±8.36%, specificity 80.74±8.28%, outperforming compared state-of-the-art and feature-selection baseline methods; selected ROIs were qualitatively linked to previously reported ASD-associated regions and subtypes. | quote: \"EAG-RS 0.760±0.033 73.71±2.83 64.56±8.36 80.74±8.28\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-067" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1209 ;
            slr:answer_text "predictive — best ABIDE hold-out accuracy 65.0% (baseline 51.6%) combining functional MRI with personal characteristic data; functional MRI alone 59.2%, structural MRI alone 60.1%, PCD alone 59.6%, structural+PCD 64.1% | quote: \"Table 16. ABIDE results summary. Data Source(s) Accuracy Sensitivity Speciﬁcity Functional MRI 59.2% 72.2% 45.4% Structural MRI 60.1% 70.4% 49.1% Personal Characteristic 59.6% 60.9% 58.3% Structural MRI + Personal Characteristic 64.1% 75.7% 51.9% Functional MRI + Personal Characteristic 65.0% 71.3% 58.3%\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:RQ5> ;
            slr:question_id "RQ5" ;
            slr:source_id "S-032" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1206 ;
            slr:answer_text """MGRL outperformed single-scale GCN and handcrafted-feature baselines on both sites: NYU accuracy 0.795±0.068/AUC 0.886±0.062; UM accuracy 0.762±0.078/AUC 0.867±0.049; improvement of at least 3% over single-atlas GCNs attributed to complementary multi-scale topology information. | quote: "MGRL (Ours)
0.795 ± 0.068
