<urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:cl6-site-handling-reported-site-covariate-harmonisation-e-g> a slr:ResearchQuestion ;
    dcterms:title "CL6 Site handling reported (site covariate, harmonisation e.g.…" ;
    slr:has_answer [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1257 ;
            slr:answer_text "Partly — no ComBat/covariate harmonisation or leave-site-out scheme is used, but the authors explicitly test for site confounding via a site-only baseline classifier and a site-balanced test-set re-evaluation, both of which argue against a site-driven result. | quote: \"We then tested those previously-trained classifiers on these new “site-balanced test sets” and found that the accuracies did not differ significantly from the original test set results: here, it was 69.88% for ADHD-200 and 63.46% for ABIDE.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:cl6-site-handling-reported-site-covariate-harmonisation-e-g> ;
            slr:source_id "S-023" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1259 ;
            slr:answer_text "No — no site covariate, harmonisation, or leave-site-out scheme is reported for the pooled 17-site cohort" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:cl6-site-handling-reported-site-covariate-harmonisation-e-g> ;
            slr:source_id "S-074" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1197 ;
            slr:answer_text "Yes — leave-one-site-out cross-validation across the four sites. | quote: \"a leave-site out cross-validation scheme was performed: each training set was composed by all the sites except one, that was left out for validation.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:cl6-site-handling-reported-site-covariate-harmonisation-e-g> ;
            slr:source_id "S-062" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1201 ;
            slr:answer_text "Yes — site (along with age, gender and handedness) was explicitly regressed out of FC weights via OLS multiple regression, following an approach from a prior ABIDE study. | quote: \"Site bias was corrected among diﬀerent sites similar to an approach described previously by an ABIDE study (Heinsfeld et al., 2018). Speciﬁcally, a multiple regression analysis was conducted to control for potentially confounding variables (site, age, gender, and handedness). These variables were regressed from FC weights across connections among ROIs. When adjusting for the confounding factors, our regression model is: y = β0 + β1x1 + β2x2 + β3x3 + β4x4 + ε where y is the vector of FC weights, x1 to x4 represent the four explanatory variables, site, age, gender, and handedness. βi is the intercept and the corresponding regression coeﬃcients. ε is the residual vector. Using ordinary least squares (OLS) estimation, βi was estimated. Then, these cofounding variables were regressed out from the FC weights.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:cl6-site-handling-reported-site-covariate-harmonisation-e-g> ;
            slr:source_id "S-025" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1250 ;
            slr:answer_text "Partly — the primary evaluation pools sites in proportion (not leave-site-out), though a supplementary per-site 5-fold cross-validation is also reported. | quote: \"Then, 5-fold cross-validation on each site is performed separately.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:cl6-site-handling-reported-site-covariate-harmonisation-e-g> ;
            slr:source_id "S-076" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1179 ;
            slr:answer_text "No" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:cl6-site-handling-reported-site-covariate-harmonisation-e-g> ;
            slr:source_id "S-070" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1171 ;
            slr:answer_text """Partly — an intra-site stratified shuffle-split cross-validation was performed to probe site effects, but this is not a leave-site-out design and no site covariate/harmonisation is used in the main pooled result | quote: "For the challenges of site-related 
variability, we also performed an intra-site prediction based on the 
stratified shuffle split cross-validation.\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:cl6-site-handling-reported-site-covariate-harmonisation-e-g> ;
            slr:source_id "S-052" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1226 ;
            slr:answer_text "No — no site covariate, harmonisation, or leave-site-out evaluation is reported; the NYU subset is analysed separately as a single-site benchmark, not as a held-out generalisation test" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:cl6-site-handling-reported-site-covariate-harmonisation-e-g> ;
            slr:source_id "S-014" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1202 ;
            slr:answer_text """No — ABIDE I (17 sites) and ABIDE II (16 sites) are pooled for the group-difference analysis with no site covariate, harmonisation, or leave-site-out evaluation reported. | quote: "This study included 1112 ABIDE I datasets 
from 17 sites and 983 ABIDE II datasets from 16 sites.\"""" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:cl6-site-handling-reported-site-covariate-harmonisation-e-g> ;
            slr:source_id "S-091" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1244 ;
            slr:answer_text "Yes | quote: \"site-out analysis (details can be found in Additional file 1: “Reproducibility” section) in the ADOS-guided fALFF and GMV fusion on the whole ASD group to check whether the site effect will contribute to current ASD pattern.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:cl6-site-handling-reported-site-covariate-harmonisation-e-g> ;
            slr:source_id "S-009" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1203 ;
            slr:answer_text "Partly — no statistical harmonisation (e.g. ComBat) is used; site heterogeneity is instead addressed via the federated-learning design itself plus two domain-adaptation strategies (Fed-MoE, Fed-Align), and Cross/Mix comparisons quantify cross-site generalisation. | quote: \"Overall, the accuracies of using CC200 was lower than the accuracies of us- ing HO. This could be caused by overﬁtting as the number of parameters required for training CC200 data is higher than HO due to the dimensionality of the input.\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:cl6-site-handling-reported-site-covariate-harmonisation-e-g> ;
            slr:source_id "S-020" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1193 ;
            slr:answer_text "Yes — ComBat harmonization applied for site effects, validated against a surface-based linear model control. | quote: \"Data were harmo­ nized for site effects while preserving effects of age and  ASD diagnosis using ComBat [86]\"" ;
            slr:answers_question <urn:synthscholar:review:review_local_20261015_abide_rsfmri:question:cl6-site-handling-reported-site-covariate-harmonisation-e-g> ;
            slr:source_id "S-080" ],
        [ a slr:ChartingQuestionAnswer ;
            slr:about_source _:n8cdf5207cb25495c891b44af156133bfb1166 ;
